2), Home Indicator (6:42), Button (6:25 clone + states), Text Field (6:28 clone).\n\nLet me first get the design context of these given components so I can replicate their exact appearance:\n- Button 6:25\n- Text Field 6:28\n- Status Bar 6:32\n- Home Indicator 6:42\n- Also a few media symbols to understand their structure (they're probably vector icons).\n\nLet me do get_design_context on 6:21 (Components frame) which will give me full detail on Button, Text Field, Status Bar, Home Indicator. And also maybe on 1:5 (Media frame) — that might be huge. Better to get individual symbols.\n\nActually, the plan: use figma.getNodeById to clone nodes. I don't strictly need to know their internal structure — cloning preserves everything. What I need to know:\n1. Their sizes (have from metadata).\n2. How to recolor icons (icons may be recolored per brief). To recolor, I'd need to modify fills of vector children. I can write a generic function that walks a node tree and sets fills on all vector/text children.\n\nLet me get design context for the Button, Text Field, Status Bar, Home Indicator to see their exact styling. Also check one icon to see its structure.\n\nLet me call get_design_context on 6:21 (components frame). That returns XML of the whole frame with all props — good.\n\nThen for media, I'll clone without needing context.\n\nLet me also check the workspace page 8:2 to see if it's empty.\n\nAfter that, I'll design the system:\n\n**Design system (light mode overall; maybe dark for trading? The brief allows light or dark per area or whole app. I'll do light mode for banking, dark mode for trading area to show range — actually consistency is scored (\"Visual quality & consistency of your own system\"). Hmm, \"light / dark mode\" listed under colors I define. I could do light for banking and dark for trading — that's a common pattern (trading apps often dark). It shows state design ability. Let me do that: Banking = light, Trading = dark. Both share brand primary #1573FE.\n\n**Colors:**\n\nBanking (light):\n- bg: #F5F7FA (light gray background)\n- surface: #FFFFFF\n- text primary: #0F1B2D (near-black navy)\n- text secondary: #6B7A90\n- text tertiary: #9AA7B8\n- divider: #E8EDF3\n- brand: #1573FE\n- brand dark text on brand: #FFFFFF\n- gain: #16A34A (green)\n- loss: #E5484D (red)\n- warning: #F59E0B\n- disabled: #C6D0DC\n- card gradient: navy gradient (#0E1B33 → #1B3A66) for payment cards\n- unread badge: #FF4D4F or loss red\n\nTrading (dark):\n- bg: #0B0F1A\n- surface: #131A2A / #161F31\n- surface alt: #1C2740\n- text primary: #F2F5FA\n- text secondary: #8A94A8\n- divider: #232D42\n- brand: #1573FE\n- gain: #22C55E (or #2EBD85 — trading green)\n- loss: #F6465D (trading red)\n\nType scale (Poppins for headings/brand, Roboto for numbers/body):\n- Display 28/34 Poppins SemiBold\n- Title 22/28 Poppins SemiBold\n- Heading 18/24 Poppins SemiBold\n- Subhead 16/22 Poppins Medium\n- Body 14/20 Roboto Regular\n- Label 12/16 Roboto Medium / Poppins Medium\n- Caption 11/14 Roboto Regular\n- Numeric large: Roboto Bold\n\nSpacing: 4/8/12/16/20/24. Screen padding 20 (banking) / 16 (trading). Radius: 16 cards, 12 inputs, 24 buttons (pill), small 8.\n\n**Layout of each frame (390×844):**\n\nCommon: Status bar at top (44px), home indicator at bottom.\n\n1. **01_Welcome** (light):\n   - Status bar\n   - Center: Illustration_Welcome (~320×380 scaled to ~300 wide), headline \"Manage your finances simply\" (Poppins SemiBold 28, center), subcopy? Brief only requires the copy \"Manage your finances simply\". Maybe add small supporting text? Copy must match \"Fixed data\" — only specified copy required. I can add minor supporting text but safer to keep minimal. Actually adding extra copy is fine as long as required copy matches. I'll keep it clean: illustration + headline + GET STARTED button + \"Already have an account?\" Log In text link at bottom.\n   - GET STARTED → primary button (342×48, brand, radius 24) → link to 02_Photo_ID.\n   - \"Already have an