ancial mobile application.\"\n   - GET STARTED button → 07_Trade_Home.\n   - Maybe background decorative gradient/coin images. Use Coin_BTC/ETH faintly? Could look nice: large coins. But careful with recoloring. I can place Coin_BTC large with low opacity as decoration.\n   - Illustration? Only welcome illustration is for banking. I'll use banners? Not required. Keep typographic + coins decoration.\n\n7. **07_Trade_Home** (dark):\n   - Header: Avatar_User, search field \"Search\", scan icon, notification icon (unread).\n   - Banners: Banner_ETH_2_0, Banner_Upcoming_Events — horizontal carousel (two banners, one full one peeking or side by side small). Banners are 300×135 → scale to 358×~90? Aspect 300:135 = 2.22. At 300 wide → 135 high. Two banners side by side won't fit; do horizontal scroll: first banner full width (358), second peeking. Actually space is tight: header, shortcuts, portfolio, exchange rates. Brief requires banners though. Let me layout:\n     - Header (avatar, search, scan, notif): ~56\n     - Shortcuts row (Deposit · Earn · Gift card · More · Orders · Referral · Save coins · Shop — 8 items, 2 rows of 4? The list: Deposit · Earn · Gift card · More · Orders · Referral · Save coins · Shop. I'll do one horizontal scroll row of 8 circular buttons, or 2 rows of 4. Horizontal scroll with ~4.5 visible.) Actually with order given: \"Deposit · Earn · Gift card · More · Orders · Referral · Save coins · Shop\" (must-include alphabetical) — data block says \"Deposit · Referral · Earn · Save coins · Orders · Shop · Gift card · More\". I'll use data block order: Deposit, Referral, Earn, Save coins, Orders, Shop, Gift card, More — 2 rows of 4.\n     - Banners: one banner row — show Banner_ETH_2_0 full width, height ~88 (scaled 300×135 → 196×88? no: 2.22 ratio → 88 high = 195 wide. Hmm too narrow.) Let me reconsider: banner 300×135 at width 358 → height 161. That's big. I could show at width 195 height 88, two side-by-side? 195+195+gap 8 = 398 > 358. Width ~175 each, height 79. That works: two banners side by side at 175×79 each. The banner graphics may have text that becomes small but acceptable. Actually banners are \"symbols\" - images. 175×79 from 300×135 is fine.\n     \n     Alternatively show first banner full-width 358×161 and second one peeking — takes more vertical space. With everything required (portfolio 4 coins, exchange rates), vertical space at 844 is tight. Let me plan vertical budget:\n     - Status bar 44\n     - Header row ~64\n     - Shortcuts 2 rows: 2×(48+20 label) + gaps ≈ 140. Hmm heavy. Alternative: 1 scrollable row of 8: 48 icon + 14 label = 70. Choose 1 row of 8 with horizontal scroll (5 visible). Saves space. But then all 8 must appear — they will, just partially off-frame. Checklist coverage might evaluate visible content... risky if cut off. 2 rows of 4 is safer: each cell 48 icon + 12 label. Rows at ~66 each → 140 total. \n     \n     Hmm, but is there a better arrangement? Shortcuts as 8 small tiles in 2 rows of 4, each tile: 40px icon in 44 tile + label 11px. Total ~130 with gaps.\n     - Banners row: 175×79 ×2 → 79 + gap.\n     - My Portfolios: title row 24 + 4 rows × 56 = 224 + see all. \n     - Exchange rates: title + horizontal chips row ~70.\n     - Bottom nav: 80.\n     Total: 44+64+140+87+252+78+80 = 745 + paddings ~60 = 805. Tight but OK at 844. \n\n     Alternative: exchange rates as compact 3 chips row (like banking). OK.\n\n     Portfolio row: coin logo 36, name+ticker, holding, value, 24h change, 7-day trend (mini sparkline). Row height 60. Need mini sparkline per coin — draw vector polyline. I'll create sparkline as vector network or use simple line via createVector with vectorPaths. Simpler: use a polyline vector with path data. 4 different sparklines (up, down, up, up).\n\n8. **08_Market** (dark):\n   - Header: title \"Market\", filter icon right.\n   - Search field \"Search coin\" + tabs: Favorites / Spot / Futures / Zones / Others, current Favorites (underline indicator).\n   - Coin list: 9 coins (BTC, ETH, USDT, BNB, ADA, XRP, SOL, DOT, AVAX) each with ticker, name, 24h volume, price, 24h change. Icons: have Coin_BTC, ETH, XRP, BNB, SOL. Missing USDT, ADA, DOT, AVAX — I need placeholder coin icons: create colored circles with ticker letter(s). For USDT: teal circle with \"T\" (₮). ADA: blue circle \"ADA\". DOT: pink circle. AVAX: red circle. Draw as ellipse + text — acceptable as \"recolor\"? These aren't brand assets in the kit; I'll create simple monogram circles. \n   - Rows: 9 × 56 = 504. Header 44+56, search 48, tabs 40, nav 80 → total ~ 44+56+8+48+12+40+8+504+80 = 800. OK.\n   - Row: logo 36, ticker bold + name secondary, volume below name? Layout: left logo; ticker+name; right: price + change; middle-right: volume. Classic: | logo | BTC/Bitcoin ... | $29,198.24 / +3.73% | Vol column. I'll do: logo, then column (ticker, Vol 2.8B), then right column (price, change). \"24h volume\" label — the data \"BTC Bitcoin $29,198.24 · +3.73% · 2.8B\" — volume 2.8B. Show \"Vol 2.8B\" under ticker. \n   - BTC row click → 10_Exchange_Crypto.\n\n9. **09_Exchange_Stock** (dark):\n   - Header: back? Brief actions: filter, swap direction, calculator. Copy \"Exchange\". Main nav current tab Exchange.\n   - Side toggle: Buy / Sell, current Buy (segmented control).\n   - From card: AAPL (Apple Inc.), Logo_Apple, amount $156.50 being entered (show cursor/underscore to indicate entering), stock changeable (chevron down). \n   - Swap button in middle (Icon_Swap).\n   - To card: SPOT (Spotify), Logo_Spotify, ≈ 0.69 shares at $226.90, stock changeable (chevron).\n   - Keypad: 1, 2 ABC, 3 DEF, 4 GHI, 5 JKL, 6 MNO, 7 PQRS, 8 TUV, 9 WXYZ, 0, backspace. 4×3 grid: 1 2 3 / 4 5 6 / 7 8 9 / . 0 backspace? Brief: 1 · 2 ABC · 3 DEF · 4 GHI · 5 JKL · 6 MNO · 7 PQRS · 8 TUV · 9 WXYZ · 0 · backspace — 11 keys. Standard: last row: (empty or .) 0 backspace. I'll do last row: \".\" empty? To be safe: row4 = [blank, 0, backspace]. Or make it 1 2 3 / 4 5 6 / 7 8 9 / backspace 0 calculator? Calculator is separate action. Keep [empty, 0, backspace].\n   - Filter icon placement: header right? or near side toggle. I'll put filter in header right. Calculator: near amount (small icon button in From card right) or next to keypad bottom? I'll put calculator icon button aligned with the \"To\" area or above keypad right. Simplest: header has filter; calculator icon button on the keypad panel header? Hmm. Let me put: header: title \"Exchange\" + filter icon. Under side toggle, From card (with calculator icon on right side of the From card header?). Actually cleaner: a row under the From/To cards: small icon buttons [filter] [calculator]? But filter in header is fine, and calculator as a small circle button in the From card's right side. Good.\n   - Main nav: Exchange tab active (center).\n\n10. **10_Exchange_Crypto** (dark):\n    - Header: pair selector BTC/USDT with Logo_BTC, chevron down (pair changeable), Vol 2.8B, last price 29,198.24, +3.73%.\n    - View toggle: Orderbook / Chart, current Orderbook.\n    - Order book: 5 asks (red, highest first: 29,203.00, 29,201.80, 29,200.65, 29,199.40, 29,198.50) then spread/last price, then 5 bids (green: 29,198.00, 29,196.75, 29,195.20, 29,194.10, 29,193.50). Each with price + amount, depth bar background.\n    - Order form: side Buy/Sell toggle (Buy active green? — trading convention: Buy green, Sell red), type Limit (changeable dropdown), price 29,198.00 USDT with −/+ steppers, amount 0.0500 BTC with −/+ steppers, percentage quick buttons 25% 50% 75% 100%, Total 1,459.90 USDT, Available 2,500.00 USDT, Buy BTC button.\n    - Main nav: Exchange tab active.\n    \n    Vertical budget: status 44, header pair 56, view toggle 36, order book: asks 5×20=100 + mid 24 + bids 5×20=100 = 224, form: ~280, nav 80. Total 44+56+36+224+280+80=720 + gaps ~40 = 760. OK. Make order book rows 18-20px, compact.\n\n**Prototype links:**\n- 01: GET STARTED → 02_Photo_ID (On Click → Navigate to)\n- 02: back → 01_Welcome; CONTINUE → 03_Bank_Home\n- 03: Transactions See all → 04_Bank_Transactions; bottom nav: Trans. → 04, Profile → 05 (Home current, no link needed but could link to self — skip); \n- 04: bottom nav: Home → 03, Profile → 05\n- 05: bottom nav: Trans. → 04, Home → 03\n- 06: GET STARTED → 07_Trade_Home\n- 07: BTC portfolio row → 10_Exchange_Crypto; bottom nav: Markets → 08, Exchange → 09\n- 08: BTC row → 10_Exchange_Crypto; bottom nav: Home → 07, Exchange → 09\n- 09: bottom nav: Home → 07, Markets → 08\n- 10: bottom nav: Home → 07, Markets → 08\n\nBrief link lists:\n- 03: \"→ Transactions entry → 04_Bank_Transactions → tabs → 04 / 03 / 05\" — tabs links: from 03, Trans. tab → 04, Profile → 05. (Home is current.)\n- 04: \"→ tabs → 04 / 03 / 05\" — Home → 03, Profile → 05.\n- 05: \"→ tabs → 04 / 03 / 05\" — Trans. → 04, Home → 03.\n- 07: \"→ BTC → 10_Exchange_Crypto → tabs → 07 / 08 / 09\" — Markets → 08, Exchange → 09.\n- 08: \"→ BTC → 10_Exchange_Crypto → tabs → 07 / 08 / 09\" — Home → 07, Exchange → 09.\n- 09: \"→ tabs → 07 / 08 / 09\" — Home → 07, Markets → 08.\n- 10: \"→ tabs → 07 / 08 / 09\" — Home → 07, Markets → 08.\n\nPrototype interactions: On Click / On Tap → Navigate to frame. Use figma.currentPage... in workspace page. For each link, create prototypeReactions on the node: node.permissions? The plugin API: node.prototypeReactions? Actually you set `reactions` on a node? The Plugin API: `node.reactions` is deprecated? Let me recall: In Figma plugin API, prototype connections are made via `node.reactions`? No — it's `prototypeReactions`? Hmm.\n\nThe Figma Plugin API: `Reaction` type, and nodes have `reactions` property? Let me recall precisely. TextNode/FrameNode etc. have `reactions: ReadonlyArray<Reaction>` — yes, `reactions` is the property (deprecated? I believe `reactions` exists and there's also `prototypeReactions` on some nodes?). \n\nFrom Figma docs: FrameNode.reactions: ReadonlyArray<Reaction>. Reaction = { action: Action, trigger: Trigger | null }. For navigation: action = { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: node.id, navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: { type: \"DISSOLVE\" | ..., duration: 0.3 } , preserveScrollPosition: false}. Trigger = { type: \"CLICK\" } (or type: \"TAP\"?). I believe trigger for click is { type: \"CLICK\" }. There's also { type: \"MOUSE_DOWN\" } etc. For prototype \"On Tap\" it's \"CLICK\"? In the plugin API, Trigger types: \"CLICK\", \"HOVER\", \"MOUSE_ENTER\", \"MOUSE_LEAVE\", \"MOUSE_DOWN\", \"MOUSE_UP\", \"AFTER_TIMEOUT\", \"KEY_DOWN\", \"DRAG\". Yes \"CLICK\" is on click/tap.\n\nSo: node.reactions = [{ trigger: { type: \"CLICK\" }, action: { type: \"NODE\", destinationId: \"3:2\", navigation: \"NAVIGATE\", transition: { type: \"SMART_ANIMATE\", duration: 0.3 }, preserveScrollPosition: false } }].\n\nTransition types: \"DISSOLVE\", \"SMART_ANIMATE\", \"MOVE_IN\", \"MOVE_OUT\", \"PUSH\", \"SLIDE_IN\", \"SLIDE_OUT\". I'll use SMART_ANIMATE 300ms where possible; simpler DISSOLVE for welcome. Fine.\n\nAlso component overrides: since I'm cloning media symbols, no need.\n\n**Component strategy:**\n\nTo satisfy \"reusable components\" scoring, I'll create components on the workspace page in a side area (e.g., x = 500+, arranged in a grid at y offsets). Components:\n\n1. Shell_StatusBar (clone of 6:32 as component — 6:32 is already a symbol/component instance? It's marked `symbol` in metadata, meaning it's an instance of a component or a component. In metadata output, `<symbol>` likely denotes COMPONENT or INSTANCE. I'll check with get_design_context or via code: figma.getNodeById(\"6:32\").type. If it's INSTANCE, I can clone instance; better to find its master component and clone that, or create a component containing a clone.\n\n2. Shell_HomeIndicator (6:42).\n\n3. Button/Primary (clone 6:25 → make component), Button/Secondary (outline), Button/Disabled? Not required explicitly, but \"All states\" evaluation. I'll define Button component with variants? Variants via componentPropertyDefinitions — creating variants: create multiple components grouped with combineAsVariants. That's doable: create Button/Default, Button/Pressed, Button/Disabled, Button/Secondary. Use combineAsVariants to make a variant component set named \"Button\".\n\nThat's a lot of work but scores \"Component reuse\" and \"State design\". Let me be pragmatic: create variant sets for Button (Default/Secondary/Disabled) and maybe Toggle/Switch. Keep others as single components with instances configured via overrides.\n\nComponents list (banking + trading):\n- Shell/Status Bar (from 6:32)\n- Shell/Home Indicator (from 6:42)\n- Button (variants: Primary, Secondary, Disabled) — from 6:25 style\n- Text Field (from 6:28)\n- Nav/Bank Tab Bar (5 tabs, with active tab property? Simpler: one component, and in each frame override colors per active tab by swapping icon/text colors on instance children — overrides on nested children allowed if not component itself. I'll build tab bar as a component with 5 tab items; per frame, set active tab by overriding the specific tab's icon fill/opacity and label color. Doable via instance.children traversal... but overriding nested text fills on an instance: allowed via instance.findOne and set properties — yes, instance children support overrides (fills, characters? characters can't be overridden on text? Actually text characters CAN be overridden in instances via setRangeCharacters... hmm, text overrides: you can override fills, fontSize, etc. on text nodes in instances. Setting characters on instance sublayers is allowed too I think (text override). But changing which tab is \"active\" involves more than fills (e.g., pill background visibility) — can override visible property. It's fine.\n  \n  Simpler alternative: build tab bar component with all 5 tabs, default state = first tab active? Then per frame override: set active tab's label fill to brand + icon full opacity, others gray. With fills overrides this works.\n\n  Even simpler: two components: \"Tab Bar/Bank\" with Home active default... but we need 3 states (Home, Trans., Profile active). I'll do the override approach.\n\n- Header/Bank (menu + title/greeting + contacts + notifications badge) — as component with overrides? Headers differ per screen (03 greeting vs 04 title vs 05). I'll make a component \"Header/Bank\" containing left icon slot? Overly generic is hard. Alternative: make smaller reusable components: Action/IconButton (circle with icon), Badge/NotificationDot, Card/Payment, Row/Transaction, Row/Rate (chip), SectionTitle, Card/Balance, Card/WeeklyChart, Card/Budget, Row/Setting, Switch/ON, Avatar/Edit, etc. Then compose headers per-frame from IconButton instances + text. That demonstrates reuse and is practical.\n\n- IconButton component (56×56 circle? or 40×40). With icon instance inside.\n- PaymentCard component (with props overridden per card: number, exp).\n- RateChip component (currency, rate, change).\n- TransactionRow component (icon, title, amount, change, date).\n- BalanceCard, WeeklyChart (frame with bars — component with static bars; selected Thu fixed, fine), BudgetCard, SettingRow (icon, label, value + optional chevron/switch), TabBarBank, TabBarTrade, CoinRow (market), PortfolioRow, Shortcut (icon+label), Banner instance (direct symbol clones), OrderBookRow (side, price, amount, depth%), StepperField (label, value, unit with − +), KeyCap (keypad), SegmentedControl (options, active), ViewToggle, PairHeader... \n\nThat's ~25 components. Realistic within effort if I write good helper functions.\n\nTo manage code size limits (50k chars per call, but practically I'll do ~10-15 calls), I'll write a helper library approach: each use_figma call is separate JS execution — variables don't persist between calls! So each call must re-define helpers or I use one big call. 50k chars limit per call. The full build might be 60-120k chars total. So split into phases, each phase self-contained with needed helpers (I can define a compact helper preamble in each call).\n\nPhases:\n1. Setup: copy media symbols into workspace as components (icon components etc.). Create a \"component strip\" on the left side (x from -500..0), and define base custom components (IconButton, Badge, Switch, SectionHeader, Button variants, Text Field clone).\n   Also clone Status Bar + Home Indicator components.\n   \n   Important: media symbols — check their type. If INSTANCE, get master via .masterComponent, then componentClone. In plugin API: `node.componentClone()`? That's for instances? No — `componentClone()` isn't a thing. InstanceNode.masterComponent gives the ComponentNode. Cloning a ComponentNode gives another ComponentNode? Actually clone() on a ComponentNode returns a ComponentNode in newer API (component nodes can be cloned; the clone becomes a component too? Historically clone of component = component? I believe ComponentNode.clone() returns a ComponentNode). Safe path: if node.type === \"INSTANCE\", use node.masterComponent.clone() (or create component from cloning the master). If node.type === \"COMPONENT\", node.clone().\n\n   Then rename e.g. \"Icon/Menu\". Also for recoloring: I'll set fills on vectors inside the component.\n\n   How do icons look (strokes vs fills)? Need get_design_context for one icon to know. E.g., 2:50 (Icon_Menu). And check status bar (6:32) to know its contents (time \"9:41\", battery etc.).\n\n2. Build frames 01, 02, 06 (welcome/photo/xtrade welcome).\n3. Build 03 (bank home) with its components (cards, rates, transactions, tab bar).\n4. Build 04 (transactions) with chart/budget components.\n5. Build 05 (profile).\n6. Build 07 (trade home) with portfolio/banner/shortcuts + tab bar trade.\n7. Build 08 (market).\n8. Build 09 (stock exchange).\n9. Build 10 (crypto exchange).\n10. Prototype links (one call): set reactions.\n11. Screenshots + fixes.\n\nFonts: must load before text: Poppins (Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold) and Roboto (Regular, Medium, Bold). Use figma.loadFontAsync for each.\n\nLet me now get design context for the components page (6:21) to see exact Button/Text Field/Status Bar styles, and one icon (2:50) to understand icon structure. Also check workspace page 8:2 content.\n\nThe get_design_context returns XML with full properties. Let me call for 6:21 and 8:2 in parallel. Also 2:50 tile icon.\n\nActually the instruction says get_metadata only gives structure; get_design_context gives implementable detail. I'll call get_design_context on 6:21, and on 8:2 (workspace - might be empty), and 2:50.\n\nLet me do that now.","signature":"49018a6a80f248bda0df525d"}],"id":"36297212-280c-41ef-81f9-a3bfa6e4b3f6","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d351031-0fa6-4945-b5e3-9a2839717795","uuid":"cc9a9ec0-97d8-4eb5-b29f-a2bcb1513a44","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:09:23.308Z","thinking_duration_ms":168672}
