{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All assets are clear now:\n- Icons: black 24×24 solid glyphs (fillable → can recolor to white/gray)\n- Logos: Apple (black), Spotify (green), Mastercard (white version - appears white/light on light bg), Coin_BTC (orange), Coin_ETH (purple), Coin_XRP (black), Coin_BNB (yellow), Coin_SOL (black/gradient)\n- Avatar_User: woman with orange hat illustration\n- Banner_ETH_2_0: dark blue banner \"Bio Chance ETH 2.0 What are The Biggest Verticals to Watch?\"\n- Banner_Upcoming_Events: yellow/orange banner \"Upcoming Events in Singapore 1-10 August 2022\"\n- Illustration_Welcome: light green/purple abstract shapes\n- ID_Card_Placeholder: blue card with avatar silhouette\n\nNote: Mastercard logo and XRP/SOL coins are black — on dark payment card they may need recolor; Mastercard appears whitish in tile (tile bg light gray, logo white?). Looks like white/light — it was rendered light gray. Hmm, actually the Logo_Mastercard tile shows a very light logo — it's probably white, designed to sit on dark card surfaces. Good for our navy cards.\n\nCoin_XRP and Coin_SOL are black — used on dark trading UI, I may need to recolor to white or put on light circular chip background. I'll put them on white circular chips in dark UI.\n\nNow let me start building. First phase: set up workspace — copy all needed media as components into the workspace page, build base components (status bar shell, buttons, etc.).\n\nPlan for Phase 1 code:\n1. Get workspace page (8:2).\n2. Load fonts (Poppins, Roboto families) — needed later; in phase 1 maybe not needed unless creating components with text. Button clone has text; status bar has text. Cloning doesn't require font loading (only editing text does). But renaming doesn't need fonts. Skip font loading in phase 1 except when needed.\n\n3. For each media symbol id, get node; if INSTANCE → masterComponent; create component by cloning master (or the node if COMPONENT). Actually simplest: \n   - const n = figma.getNodeById(id)\n   - let comp\n   - if (n.type === \"COMPONENT\") comp = n.clone()\n   - else if (n.type === \"INSTANCE\") { comp = n.masterComponent.clone() } — wait, ComponentNode.clone() returns ComponentNode? In the plugin API, ComponentNode.clone() does return a ComponentNode. Yes.\n   - else (FRAME/GROUP) → wrap: create component from node? There's figma.createComponentFromNode(node) which converts/clones any node into a component. That's the universal approach: figma.createComponentFromNode(n.clone() if needed). createComponentFromNode works on FrameNode, GroupNode, ComponentNode, InstanceNode? For an instance it converts to component. Let me just use figma.createComponentFromNode(n) — but careful: it MOVES the node? createComponentFromNode(node) creates a new component from the node — it reparents the original node. That would break the reference page! Docs: \"createComponentFromNode(node) — Creates a new component from node. The resulting component is placed in the same parent as node, at the same position.\" It reparents/mutates the original. To be safe: clone first, then createComponentFromNode(clone). The clone lands in same parent (media page) then I move it to workspace. \n\n   Wait — cloning a symbol/instance and converting: if the source is an INSTANCE, cloning gives INSTANCE; createComponentFromNode(instanceClone) → converts to COMPONENT. Good.\n\n4. Recolor icons: for icon components (24×24 glyphs), write function recolor(node, color) { walk children; if fills editable, set solid fill color; also strokes }. Icon glyphs are likely fills-based vectors. I'll set fills on all descendants that have fills !== [] and type VECTOR/BOOLEAN/TEXT.\n\n5. Create component organization: place all components on workspace page in a column at x = -600 (left of frames area), grouped in frames labeled \"Library\". Actually components can't be inside auto-layout unless... they can be anywhere. I'll lay them out manually at positions. Or simpler: place each component node at computed grid positions on workspace page (x: -800..0, y: 0..1500). Frames of the app start at x=0? I'll put app frames in a row starting at x=0, y=0 with 100px gaps, 2 rows. Components at x = -1000.. -100. Hmm, negative coords fine.\n\nLayout plan for workspace page:\n- App frames: row 1 (y=0): 01_Welcome (x=0), 02_Photo_ID (x=490), 03_Bank_Home (x=980), 04_Bank_Transactions (x=1470), 05_Profile (x=1960)\n- Row 2 (y=1000): 06_XTrade_Welcome (x=0), 07_Trade_Home (x=490), 08_Market (x=980), 09_Exchange_Stock (x=1470), 10_Exchange_Crypto (x=1960)\n- Library zone: x from -1400 to -200, y 0..~1600. Components arranged in labeled group frames.\n\nPhase 1: clone media into components (icons ×37, logos ×8, images ×5) + clone Button/TextField/StatusBar/HomeIndicator as base. That's ~54 nodes. One call, fine. Store mapping id→new component id. I'll need the mapping in later phases! Since variables don't persist, I'll find components by name in later calls: page.findOne(n => n.type === \"COMPONENT\" && n.name === \"Icon/Menu\"). To make lookup easy, name components systematically:\n- Icons: \"Icon/Tab Transactions\", etc. Or keep original names \"Icon_Menu\". Lookup by exact name among COMPONENT nodes on workspace page. Keep original names for simplicity: \"Icon_Menu\" as component name. But multiple components with same name? No, all unique.\n\nNaming: keep source names exactly (Icon_Menu, Coin_BTC, Avatar_User...). Then in later phases: findComponent(name) = page.findOne(c => c.type === \"COMPONENT\" && c.name === name && c.parent === page)? Components may be inside group frames on the page. findOne is recursive — fine.\n\nFor instances: comp.createInstance().\n\nPhase 1 also: recolor plan. Default icon color: I'll leave the component itself black; recolor per-instance by setting fills on instance's vector children (overrides). For instances, setting nested vector fills works.\n\nBut careful: some icons might use strokes. I'll handle both in recolor helper.\n\nAlso there may be multi-color icons? They look solid black. Coin icons are multicolor (brand) — don't recolor coins. Logos: Apple black, Spotify green, Mastercard white — don't recolor.\n\nNow the status bar (6:32) and home indicator (6:42): clone as components named \"Shell/Status Bar\" and \"Shell/Home Indicator\". Status bar content is black — on dark trading frames I need white version: recolor instance children to white. If the status bar has an image (battery might be vector), recolor handles vectors.\n\nText Field (6:28): clone as component \"Text Field\" (default light). For dark theme search field on 07/08, I'll build custom dark TextField component \"Text Field/Dark\" myself.\n\nButton (6:25): clone as \"Button/Primary\". It contains text \"GET STARTED\" (uppercase, letterSpacing). I'll create additional button components myself: \"Button/Secondary\" (white bg, brand text, border), \"Button/Disabled\" (gray). To match style, I'll clone the primary and modify (change fills). Font in button: need to know which font — check via get_design_context? Let me just read properties in code during phase 1 and adjust text via characters (requires font load: load fonts used: Poppins + Roboto all styles I might use).\n\nLet me now also read the exact design context of Button 6:25 and Text Field 6:28 and Status Bar 6:32 to replicate precisely. get_design_context on 6:21 gives all. Let me call it (XML). It might be large but useful. Actually, I'll skip reading full XML — instead, in phase 1 code, I'll clone them and read/adjust properties programmatically, printing key info (fills, fonts, radius) to console for me to use. The use_figma tool returns console output. Good approach: phase 1 = clone assets + inspect button/textfield/statusbar internals (print details).\n\nLet me write Phase 1 code now.\n\nPhase 1 code sketch:\n\n```js\nconst page = figma.getNodeById(\"8:2\"); // workspace\nconst ids = [ ...icon ids..., logo ids, image ids ];\nconst results = {};\nfunction srcComponent(id){\n  let n = figma.getNodeById(id);\n  if(!n) return null;\n  let base = n.type === \"INSTANCE\" ? n.masterComponent : n;\n  let c = base.clone();\n  if(c.type !== \"COMPONENT\"){ c = figma.createComponentFromNode(c); }\n  page.appendChild(c);\n  return c;\n}\nconst names = {\n \"2:7\":\"Icon_Tab_Transactions\", ... // id->name from metadata actually names already on nodes; use node.name\n};\n```\n\nI'll iterate a list of ids, clone, name = original name, position in grid, and log id map. Positions: grid cells 100 wide, 80 tall, 8 per row, starting x=-1400, y=0. Log \"name -> newId\".\n\nIcons to include (all): 2:7,2:12,2:17,2:22,2:27,2:32,2:37,2:42,2:50,2:55,2:60,2:65,2:70,2:75,2:80,2:85,2:90,2:95,2:103,2:108,2:113,2:118,2:123,2:128,2:133,2:138,4:7,4:12,4:17,4:22,4:27,4:32,4:37,4:42,4:47,4:52,4:57,4:62,4:67,4:72,4:77,4:82,4:87,4:92,4:97,4:102,4:107,4:112 (49 icons)\nLogos: 4:120,4:126,4:129,4:132,4:135,4:138,4:141,4:144 (8)\nImages: 4:150 (120 avatar), 4:153 banner ETH (300×135), 4:156 banner events (300×135), 5:2 illustration (320×380), 5:5 ID card (342×216) (5)\nShell: 6:32 status bar, 6:42 home indicator\nButton 6:25, TextField 6:28.\n\nTotal 65 clones. One call might be heavy but OK. Note: cloning instance of status bar etc fine.\n\nAlso print info about Button internals: children types, fills, cornerRadius, fontName, fontSize, letterSpacing of text, fill colors. And status bar children. I'll log JSON summary.\n\nImportant: figma.getNodeById may need await? It's sync (deprecated in favor of getNodeByIdAsync, but sync still works... The instructions say \"MUST NEVER use loadAllPagesAsync, setPluginData, createImageAsync\". getNodeById sync is fine but might be deprecated; use figma.getNodeByIdAsync? In plugin API, getNodeByIdAsync exists. The MCP tool code runs with figma global; sync version available. I'll use await figma.getNodeByIdAsync to be safe. Actually mixing: in loops with await, fine.\n\nAlso createComponentFromNode: sync. OK.\n\nOne concern: cloning INSTANCE of a component whose file is this same file — masterComponent accessible. Good.\n\nLet me also decide: for coins in dark UI, I'll wrap in white circle chips at frame level (not recolor).\n\nPhase 1 code (must be < 50000 chars, fine). Also after cloning, print compact map.\n\nThen Phase 2: create base custom components:\n- recolor icons? I'll do recolor at instance level later.\n- Build: \"Btn/Primary\" (use cloned 6:25 - rename \"Button/Primary\"), \"Button/Secondary\", \"Button/Disabled\" clones with modifications.\n- \"Chip/Tag\"? as needed.\n- IconButton (frame 40×40 circle, icon instance 24 centered) — component \"Icon Button\" with default icon Icon_Menu.\n- Badge dot component.\n- Switch ON component.\n- SectionHeader (title + \"See all\" link) — banking light version; trading dark version.\n- Tab bars: build in phase of frames? They're components: \"Tab Bar/Bank\" (light), \"Tab Bar/Trade\" (dark). Each 390×84 with 5 items. Build once, instance everywhere, override active tab colors.\n\nI'll create these in phase 2 with fonts loaded.\n\nThen phases 3-9 build frames. Phase 10: prototype. Phase 11: screenshots.\n\nTime to write Phase 1. I'll include a recolor helper and also pre-recolor: Logo_Mastercard must be visible on navy card — check its current color (might be white already). I'll log its fills.\n\nAlso check Illustration_Welcome size 320×380 and ID card 342×216 — images are symbols (instances). Their internal structure might be frames with vectors — fine as is.\n\nLet me write the code. I'll keep console output compact: log each \"name:newId\" joined.\n\nOne more consideration: the cloned Button (6:25) — instance? `<symbol>` in metadata = component or instance. I'll handle generically.\n\nAfter phase 1, I'll know component IDs; but for later phases I'll look up by name via findOne — safer regardless.\n\nEdge: createComponentFromNode on a clone of instance — the clone of an instance is an instance; createComponentFromNode(instance) → creates component. I think that works. Alternative for instances: c = inst.masterComponent.clone() (component clone). Both paths OK — I'll prefer masterComponent.clone() when instance, then it's already COMPONENT type; if clone() of ComponentNode returns ComponentNode — yes.\n\nHmm wait — actually ComponentNode.clone() historically returned a FrameNode?? No... In the plugin API, cloning a ComponentNode gives you another ComponentNode. Confirmed in docs: \"clone(): ComponentNode\". Good.\n\nLet me also load fonts at start of each phase that creates text: Poppins Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold, Roboto Regular/Medium/Bold. loadFontAsync for each.\n\nWrite Phase 1 now. Also I'll set page backgrounds? The workspace page canvas color default. Fine.\n\nCode:\n\n```js\nconst W = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"8:2\");\nconst iconIds = [\"2:7\",\"2:12\",\"2:17\",\"2:22\",\"2:27\",\"2:32\",\"2:37\",\"2:42\",\"2:50\",\"2:55\",\"2:60\",\"2:65\",\"2:70\",\"2:75\",\"2:80\",\"2:85\",\"2:90\",\"2:95\",\"2:103\",\"2:108\",\"2:113\",\"2:118\",\"2:123\",\"2:128\",\"2:133\",\"2:138\",\"4:7\",\"4:12\",\"4:17\",\"4:22\",\"4:27\",\"4:32\",\"4:37\",\"4:42\",\"4:47\",\"4:52\",\"4:57\",\"4:62\",\"4:67\",\"4:72\",\"4:77\",\"4:82\",\"4:87\",\"4:92\",\"4:97\",\"4:102\",\"4:107\",\"4:112\"];\nconst logoIds = [\"4:120\",\"4:126\",\"4:129\",\"4:132\",\"4:135\",\"4:138\",\"4:141\",\"4:144\"];\nconst imgIds = [\"4:150\",\"4:153\",\"4:156\",\"5:2\",\"5:5\"];\nconst shellIds = [\"6:32\",\"6:42\",\"6:25\",\"6:28\"];\n\nasync function toComponent(id, x, y){\n  const n = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  if(!n){ return id+\":MISSING\"; }\n  let c;\n  if(n.type === \"COMPONENT\"){ c = n.clone(); }\n  else if(n.type === \"INSTANCE\"){ c = n.masterComponent.clone(); }\n  else { c = figma.createComponentFromNode(n.clone()); }\n  // if still not component (e.g. frame clone became?) \n  if(c.type !== \"COMPONENT\"){ c = figma.createComponentFromNode(c); }\n  c.name = n.name;\n  W.appendChild(c);\n  c.x = x; c.y = y;\n  return n.name + \":\" + c.id;\n}\n\nconst out = [];\nlet col = 0, row = 0;\nconst cellW = 120, cellH = 90, x0 = -1500, y0 = 0, perRow = 10;\nasync function place(id){\n  const x = x0 + col*cellW, y = y0 + row*cellH;\n  const r = await toComponent(id, x, y);\n  out.push(r);\n  col++; if(col >= perRow){ col = 0; row++; }\n}\nfor(const id of iconIds) await place(id);\nrow += 1; col = 0;\nfor(const id of logoIds) await place(id);\nrow += 2; col = 0;\nfor(const id of imgIds) await place(id);\nrow += 5; col = 0;\nfor(const id of shellIds) await place(id);\n\n// inspect button, textfield, statusbar\nasync function info(id){\n  const n = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id);\n  const target = n.type===\"INSTANCE\" ? n.masterComponent : n;\n  const desc = { name: target.name, w: target.width, h: target.height, fills: target.fills, radius: target.cornerRadius, strokes: target.strokes, strokeWeight: target.strokeWeight, children: [] };\n  for(const ch of target.children){\n    const d = { t: ch.type, name: ch.name, x: ch.x, y: ch.y, w: ch.width, h: ch.height, fills: ch.fills, strokes: ch.strokes, radius: ch.cornerRadius };\n    if(ch.type === \"TEXT\"){ d.font = JSON.stringify(ch.fontName); d.size = ch.fontSize; d.chars = ch.characters; d.ls = JSON.stringify(ch.letterSpacing); d.align = ch.textAlignHorizontal; }\n    desc.children.push(d);\n  }\n  return desc;\n}\nconst infos = [];\nfor(const id of [\"6:25\",\"6:28\",\"6:32\",\"6:42\"]) infos.push(await info(id));\nconsole.log(\"CLONES: \" + out.join(\" | \"));\nconsole.log(\"INFO: \" + JSON.stringify(infos));\n```\n\nWait — issue: cloning components that live in the reference pages and moving them to my workspace: allowed? These are just copies; originals stay. Yes.\n\nIssue: createComponentFromNode exists in plugin API (figma.createComponentFromNode). Yes.\n\nPotential problem: the media symbols are instances — masterComponent.clone() — the master may live on the reference page; cloning gives component with proper content. Good.\n\nCareful: cloning a COMPONENT and then appendChild to workspace page — moves it there. Good.\n\nletterSpacing JSON serialization might fail on functions? letterSpacing = {value, unit} — fine with JSON.stringify. fills may include paints — fine. But if fills is the symbol \"figma.mixed\"? JSON.stringify on mixed returns null? figma.mixed is a unique symbol; JSON.stringify gives null? It's a symbol → JSON.stringify(symbol) = undefined → key dropped. Fine.\n\nAlso for text nodes, fontName might be figma.mixed if mixed styles. OK.\n\nLet me also verify workspace page id \"8:2\" is the page node itself (canvas id=\"8:2\" — yes it's the page).\n\nRun Phase 1.","signature":"eb37397322b54b2fa135a845"}],"id":"526abc6e-bf37-4f26-a540-4fea60eed2cc","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d351031-0fa6-4945-b5e3-9a2839717795","uuid":"52150067-e970-4b1b-a0cc-bfdba1c45aa8","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:11:40.634Z","thinking_duration_ms":89061}
