an + notif. Search field ~ 180×40 dark.\n27. \"Sparkline\" — vector components (4 shapes) — I'll create 4 sparkline components \"Spark/Up1\" etc. as plain polylines. Or draw inline per row. Component per shape: Spark/A (up), Spark/B (down), Spark/C (up2), Spark/D (up3). Colors gain/loss.\n28. \"Coin Placeholder\" circles for USDT/ADA/DOT/AVAX — colored circle 32 with letter text. Components \"Coin/USDT\" etc. USDT: #26A17B with \"₮\" — use \"T\". ADA: #0033AD \"ADA\"? letter \"A\"? Use ticker text small. DOT #E6007A, AVAX #E84142. Text white Roboto Bold 12/10.\n29. \"Greeting Block\"? inline.\n\nThat's a lot; I'll create most in one big phase-2 call with helper functions, then frames in separate calls. Careful with the 50k char limit per call. Phase 2 maybe ~12k chars. OK.\n\nAlso \"all rates\" entry, \"See all\" links are text instances — no links needed (entry only).\n\nLet me define helper functions for phase 2:\n\n```js\nconst W = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"8:2\");\nconst C = {}; // name->component lookup\nfunction comp(name){ return W.findOne(n => n.type===\"COMPONENT\" && n.name===name); }\nasync function loadFonts(){ for(const f of [[\"Poppins\",\"Regular\"],[\"Poppins\",\"Medium\"],[\"Poppins\",\"SemiBold\"],[\"Poppins\",\"Bold\"],[\"Roboto\",\"Regular\"],[\"Roboto\",\"Medium\"],[\"Roboto\",\"Bold\"],[\"Inter\",\"Semi Bold\"]]) await figma.loadFontAsync({family:f[0],style:f[1]}); }\nconst hex=(h,o=1)=>{const n=parseInt(h.slice(1),16);return {type:\"SOLID\",color:{r:((n>>16)&255)/255,g:((n>>8)&255)/255,b:(n&255)/255},opacity:o};};\nfunction solid... \nfunction txt(parent,chars,font,size,color,x,y,opts) -> create text node\nfunction box(parent,x,y,w,h,r,fill,stroke,sw) -> rectangle/frame\nfunction icirc(...) icon button\nfunction inst(name,parent,x,y) -> component.createInstance()\nfunction recolor(node,paint) recursive\nfunction vline/sparkline(parent,points,color,x,y,w,h,sw)\n```\n\nText nodes: set textAutoResize \"WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT\" default; for fixed boxes use \"NONE\" with resize. I'll mostly auto-size and position.\n\nFor letter spacing: t.letterSpacing = {unit:\"PERCENT\", value: X}.\n\nLine height: t.lineHeight = {unit:\"PIXELS\", value: X}.\n\nShadows: effects = [{type:\"DROP_SHADOW\", color:{r,g,b,a}, offset:{x:0,y:8}, radius:24, spread:0, visible:true, blendMode:\"NORMAL\"}].\n\nGradient fills: {type:\"GRADIENT_LINEAR\", gradientTransform:[[cos,sin,tx],[-sin,cos,ty]], gradientStops:[{position:0,color:{r,g,b,a}},...]}. For diagonal gradient on 300×180 card: gradientTransform [[0.7,0.7,-0.2],[-0.7,0.7,0.5]] approx. Simpler: use two stops horizontal-ish: [[1,0,0],[0,1,0]] = left-to-right. Diagonal: [[0.707,0.707,-0.2],[-0.707,0.707,0.5]]. I'll use that.\n\nNow positions for components in library: continue grid at y rows below current. Current clones occupy rows 0..~13 at y0=0, cellH 90 → up to y≈1170+, x -1500..-370. Images at rows ~15-20 (y 1350-1800). Shells at rows 21+ (y ~1890+). I'll place new components in a second column block: x0 = -1500, y0 = 2100 onward. Or organize: I'll just append at computed grid: startX=-1500, startY=2000, cellW=200, cellH=110, 8 per row. Some components are wide (Tab bars 390×84) — grid cells may overlap; acceptable in a workshop area (it's just library). Better: group components visually by placing with row heights per type. It's not evaluated visually, but let me keep tidy: I'll place tab bars separately.\n\nPhase 2 list (create + name):\nA. Buttons (rename clone \"Button\" → \"Btn/Primary\"; clone twice → Secondary, Disabled with modifications)\n   - Secondary: fills [white], strokes [brand 1], text fill brand.\n   - Disabled: fills [#B9C4D4], text fill white opacity 1? maybe #F0F4F8.\nB. Input: rename clone → \"Input/Light\".\nC. \"Icon Btn\": component 40×40 radius 20 white fill + shadow subtle; insert Icon_Menu instance 24 at 8,8 named \"icon\". For dark: \"Icon Btn/Dark\" fill #1A2232.\nD. \"Badge Dot\": 9×9 circle #F04438 with 1.5 white stroke.\nE. \"Switch/On\": 44×26