ance whose name contains \"txnHead\" or I named them. Safer: find by name via findOne on the frame; the link child inside Section Head instance is named \"link\". In frame 03: const txnHead = f3.findOne(n=>n.name===\"txnHead\") — did I name it? In the build (prior session) I named heads; from summary: 'txnHead \"Transactions\" at 16,522'. I believe I set names \"txnHead\" etc. Risk: name mismatch. I'll write defensive code: try several candidate names and also fallback: find instance whose child \"title\" has characters \"Transactions\".\n\nBetter approach: in wiring code, do:\nfunction headByTitle(frame, txt){ const insts = frame.findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"); return insts.find(i=>{const t=i.findOne(x=>x.name===\"title\"&&x.type===\"TEXT\"); return t&&t.characters===txt;}); }\n\nFor nav tabs: nav instance child \"t0\".. For trade nav: t0/t1/t2. For bank nav: t0..t4.\n\nFor 07 pf0: portfolio row instances named? In 07 build, rows named likely \"pf0\"..\"pf3\" or \"row0\"... uncertain. Use findAll INSTANCE with child \"ticker\" characters \"BTC\". For 08 coin0: instance with child ticker \"BTC\".\n\nWrite generic helpers:\n- byId(id)\n- destIds: F01:12:2, F02:12:22, F03:13:2, F04:14:2, F05:15:2, F06:17:2, F07:17:26, F08:18:453, F09:20:56, F10:24:2\n- function nav(frame, nodeName) => frame.findOne(n=>n.name===nodeName) — for nav instance: const nav=f.findOne(n=>n.name===\"nav\"); then nav.findOne(n=>n.name===\"t0\").\n- reactions setter: function link(node, destId){ node.reactions=[{trigger:{type:\"CLICK\"},action:{type:\"NODE\",destinationId:destId,navigation:\"NAVIGATE\",transition:{type:\"SMART_ANIMATE\",duration:0.3},preserveScrollPosition:false}}]; }\n\nPotential issue: setting reactions on nodes inside instances — allowed as override. If it errors, fallback: set on the instance itself. I'll wrap in try/catch and report results, with fallback to parent instance.\n\nAlso the brief may require more links (e.g., 05 more). The summary's pending list is authoritat