{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API schema in this environment differs from the classic Plugin API docs. From the validation error:\n\nTrigger: type \"ON_CLICK\" (not \"CLICK\").\nAction NODE type: validation says for action.type \"NODE\" — wait, it says Invalid enum value. Expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE', received 'NODE' — hmm, that's one branch. Other branches: \"CONDITIONAL\", \"URL\", \"UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME\", \"SET_VARIABLE\", \"SET_VARIABLE_MODE\". But it also validated transition within the NODE branch: \"Expected [0].action.transition to be one of the following... Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'SMART_ANIMATE'... Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing ... direction ... matchLayers\".\n\nHmm, that suggests the NODE action branch isn't listed in this message (the branch that got transition validation is probably a navigation action type that IS allowed but with different literal). The error lists candidate unions; the branch checking transition with MOVE_IN etc. — \"NAVIGATE\" action type. So action.type should be \"NAVIGATE\" with destinationId, transition {type:\"SLIDE_IN\"/..., direction, matchLayers?, easing}.\n\nWait, actually in newer plugin API typings: Action = { type: \"NAVIGATE\", destinationId, navigation, transition, preserveScrollPosition } — hmm but the error says action.type \"NODE\" invalid, expected 'BACK' | 'CLOSE' for that enum branch... The listed branches:\n1. CONDITIONAL (with conditionalBlocks)\n2. BACK | CLOSE\n3. URL (url)\n4. UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME (mediaAction)\n5. ... variants\n6. a branch with transition validated — likely \"NAVIGATE\" or \"CHANGE_TO\" — the transition error appeared nested inside one branch. The transition branch expects type MOVE_IN|MOVE_OUT|PUSH|SLIDE_IN|SLIDE_OUT with direction, matchLayers, easing. Hmm but SMART_ANIMATE/DISSOLVE should also be valid transition types in Figma API... In the RES