omponent: white circle + shadow + child \"icon\". When I created instances I may have... In 02/03/04/05 builds I used iconBtn(f,...) helper which created instance, then swapped \"icon\" child to the media icon and recolored. If recolor walked the WHOLE instance including the white circle fill... recolor skips FRAME/COMPONENT/INSTANCE nodes but the instance's direct vector children — wait the circle itself IS the component's root child? Icon Btn component = FRAME? or ellipse? If component root frame has fill white and child \"icon\" — recolor(n,paint) called on the icon child only should be fine.\n\nBut they render BLACK. Maybe the icons I swapped in (Icon_Menu, Icon_Contacts, Icon_Notification, Icon_History, Icon_More) are dark/black filled shapes — by design they might be black glyphs (from the media page, icons may be black). If the media icons are black glyphs, then on white circle they'd appear as dark glyphs — but at 237px wide thumbnail, a 40px circle with dark glyph might just look dark. In 05 screenshot, the three top buttons look like solid dark squares — not circles with glyphs. Hmm, they look like rounded dark blobs. Possibly the recolor(...) painted the icon's glyph white while circle white → but they're dark...\n\nWait, look at 05's top right: three dark squares. And 04: dark squares. 03: dark squares. 02: single dark blob top-left. So ALL Icon Btn instances look dark. Also setting rows' chevrons in 05 show as dark squares too (right side of each row shows dark rounded squares instead of light gray chevrons!). And the setting row \"tiles\" (icon 44 at 10,14) — they render as solid BLUE squares. Hmm, the Setting Row tile color should be... In Setting Row component I made tile #EAF2FF with icon? In screenshot they're saturated blue squares.\n\nAnd Txn Row tiles in 03: blue squares. Chip/Rate: fine. Pay Card: fine. Nav bar: fine (icons visible in tabs, active blue, labels visible). Portfolio? not in this row.\n\nHypothesis: The media icons are actually FILLED square-ish glyphs (e.g., the icon SVGs are solid rounded-square shapes, not line glyphs)? No — in the nav bar, tab icons render correctly (small glyphs visible: Home icon, etc.). So media icons work in nav.\n\nDifference: nav icons were swapped via `swap()` then NOT recolored (bank nav override recolored children though...). Hmm, nav in 03: for t0..t4 I recolored children with #98A2B3/#1573FE. They look fine.\n\nIcon Btn: I swapped \"icon\" child and called recolor(icn,...)? The helper iconBtn: \"instance + rescale + recolor\". If recolor target color was brand/dark and the glyph is a filled rounded square shape... no.\n\nAlternatively the issue: Icon Btn component's child \"icon\" slot originally contains some default icon instance; when I swapped to e.g. Icon_Menu (which might be 24×24 with its own colors), then recolor with white/brand... The rendering shows dark blob covering the whole 40px button — as if the swapped icon instance is HUGE (covering the button) and dark. Icon_Menu original size maybe 24×24? If original is e.g. 100×100 and I rescaled wrong... In iconBtn helper maybe I didn't rescale. A 40px slot with a 24px icon should be fine.\n\nLook closer at 02: top-left blob is a black circle with tiny white square inside? Actually it looks like a dark circle. The viewfinder below has blue corner brackets — good.\n\nLet me think about what Icon Btn component contains: \"Icon Btn (40 circle white+shadow, child 'icon')\". If in phase 2a I built Icon Btn as: frame 40×40 r20 white + instance child \"icon\" (some default media icon). When I create an instance and swap its \"icon\" child with Icon_Menu: swapComponent preserves slot size 24×24 then I rescale(24/width)? The helper ic() did rescale by scale param.\n\nBut WAIT — the rendering shows the entire button dark. What if recolor(sb, S(\"#FFFFFF\")) in statusBar... no, that's status bar.\n\nWhat if my recolor in iconBtn was applied to the BUTTON instance root: recolor(instance, paint) — walk children; the \"icon\" child is INSTANCE type → skipped; the button frame is root — root not visited (walk visits children only, root skipped). Circle stays white. Icon glyph stays its own colors. So a black glyph icon on white circle = dark glyph. At small scale could read as \"dark blob\" if the glyph is bold/filled. The media icons like Icon_Menu (hamburger) at 24px would show 3 lines, not a blob.\n\nHmm, but 05's chevrons: Setting Row \"chev\" is Icon_Chevron_Right 16px recolored? In screenshot, right side of each row = dark rounded square ~16px. A chevron glyph is a thin arrow — would NOT look like a filled square. So something's wrong with how these instances render: they render as dark filled rounded-rectangles.\n\nAH WAIT. I bet I know! The icons on 04·Media might each be built as a FRAME with a background fill (a tile!) containing the glyph. If Icon_Chevron_Right is a frame with dark fill + white glyph inside... no, in nav they render as glyphs...\n\nHold on, in nav bar the icons are ALSO instances of media icons (Icon_Tab_Home etc.) and they render as proper glyphs (I can see Home glyph, wallet glyph in tab bar). So media icons are glyphs, not tiles.\n\nAlternative hypothesis: the swapped-in icons became BLACK SQUARES because swapComponent into a slot triggers... no.\n\nLet me look again at 04 screenshot top area: left icon = dark rounded square; center-left = dark rounded square; right = dark rounded square. In 03: three dark squares. These are ~40px buttons rendered dark navy/black. That matches Icon Btn/Dark color #1A2232! Did I accidentally use Icon Btn/Dark for the light frames?? No wait — in 05 right side there are THREE dark squares and in row the chevrons dark too.\n\nOR: maybe the \"Icon Btn\" white component actually has fill... let me recall phase 2a: \"Icon Btn (40 circle white+shadow, child 'icon')\". But in the screenshots the buttons look like dark rounded SQUARES not circles. 40×40 with r20 = circle. The blobs look square-ish with slight rounding. So these may not be my Icon Btn at all — maybe they're the SWAPPED ICON rendered at 40×40 with a dark fill and rounded corners? If Icon_History etc. from media page are themselves frames with dark bg? \n\nHmm — but nav icons render fine...\n\nDifference between nav icons and top-bar icons: nav icons I recolored children (recursive) — top-bar icons I may have recolored with brand/white and they're dark... \n\nActually! Another idea: these dark blobs might be instances where swap FAILED to preserve size — e.g., the swapped icon is 40×40 because the media icon's default size is large (like 512×512) and I rescaled by 24/width but width returned stale value? A 40×40 render of a black glyph scaled down could look like a blob.\n\nI can't resolve by speculation — I'll inspect the actual nodes. But first, look at remaining issues in row 1:\n\n03: Txn tiles = solid blue squares (44×44 #1573FE?) — component tile should be #EAF2FF. Screenshot shows saturated blue. So tile recolor happened? In 03 build: `setTxt...; swap tile>icon...` — I didn't recolor tile. Component default #EAF2FF is very light blue... the screenshot tiles are clearly medium blue. Weird. Unless the swapped icon (Icon_Car_Loan etc.) fills the whole 44 tile with blue? If the loan icons are 44×44 dark glyphs... maybe. The tiles look uniform blue → likely the icon instance is 44×44 solid-ish blue shape (rounded). The loan icons might be \"filled illustrations\" from media page.\n\nSimilarly Setting Row tiles in 05: blue squares 44×44. And the chevrons: dark squares 16×16.\n\nSo pattern: swapped media icons render as SOLID RECTANGLES of their own fill color. I.e., the media icons are not line glyphs but... no wait, nav tab icons render as glyphs.\n\nHmm, actually do they? In 03 nav: \"Trans.\" tab icon — I see a small light glyph. Home tab: blue glyph. Looks like glyphs. In 05 Profile tab: blue glyph person. OK.\n\nSo why do top-bar icons/tiles/chevrons render solid? KEY DIFFERENCE: nav tab icons were NOT swapped — they're the ORIGINAL component children (Icon Btn's default icon vs nav's built-in icons). In nav Tab Bar component, the icons are media icon instances placed directly in the component. In Icon Btn, the default child is some icon, and I SWAPPED it via swapComponent. Maybe swapComponent into an instance slot renders the swapped instance at its natural size, and my rescale didn't happen or used wrong numbers, so e.g. Icon_Chevron_Right renders 16×16... still a chevron shape, not a square!\n\nUnless... the swapped icon's fill got recolored via my recolor() walker in a way that filled its frame background. recolor skips FRAME/GROUP/COMPONENT/TEXT/INSTANCE nodes but paints other nodes with existing paints. If the media icon = frame containing vector strokes... strokes recolored fine.\n\nI keep speculating. INSPECT: use_figma read-only on 05: find Setting Row instance, check chev node: type, size, fills, children. Also Icon Btn instance on 03: check \"icon\" child size/fills. And Txn Row tile + icon. Also check what Icon_Chevron_Right component looks like (fills/strokes).\n\nRow 1 other observations:\n- 03: top-left blob overlaps status bar time? The menu icon at y56 — fine. Second card peek shows \"541...\" number and chip — ok. Badge dot on notif — visible (red dot). Greeting good. Rates chips: \"AUD $0.80 +0.03 (+3.9%)\" — but screenshot shows \"+0.03 (+3.9%)\" in green small — ok. Transactions rows: title/date/amount/red chg — visible. Nav labels visible.\n- 04: Balance card, Transactions chart card w/ tooltip \"$134.90\" on Thu bar, day labels, budget card with two rows + mini bars. Nav Trans active blue. Top icons dark blobs. Chart bars: Wed 03 bar is tallest (110) but tooltip sits on Thu 04 bar (85 high)... The plan: heights [35,76,110,49,21,85], selected Thu (i=3, h=49)? Wait tooltip at x167 which is over Thu (i=3: bx=24+3*54=186, center 208?). Hmm tooltip at 167,118 and the highlighted bar in screenshot is Thu (4th). Bar heights: Mon35 Tue76 Wed110 Thu49?? In screenshot, highlighted (blue) bar is 4th, medium height, tooltip above it. But Wed (110) is tallest and unselected — that's per plan (Thu selected). Visually fine, tooltip \"$134.90\" positioned above Thu bar. OK.\n- Weekly card: \"$1,041.90\" bold + Week pill — visible.\n- 05: Account card fine (avatar, edit badge, contacts). Settings rows: labels left, values right (English, Light mode), Notifications switch ON blue — visible! Good. But chevrons dark squares, tiles blue squares.\n- 05 nav: Profile active blue at right. Good.\n\nSo the main visual bug: swapped media icons inside slots render as solid rounded rectangles. This affects:\n- 02: back button icon (Icon_Back) → blob\n- 03: menu/contacts/notif icons → blobs; txn row icons → blue squares\n- 04: history/currency/notif → blobs\n- 05: history/more/notif → blobs; setting row tiles → blue squares; chevrons → dark squares\n- 07/08/09/10: Icon Btn/Dark with Icon_Filter/Scan/Calculator/Swap icons; Shortcut Tile icons; Coin Row logos (Coin_XRP etc. - but those are fine as circles?); Stepper minus/plus (manual, fine); Key/Del icon; order book none; Tab Bar/Trade center icon (built-in, fine).\n\nWait, but in 09/10 the icons were swapped into Icon Btn/Dark via swap() too — same potential issue.\n\nHmm wait, actually let me reconsider: maybe the issue is NOT swap but RESCALE. ic() helper: instance created from media icon component at original size, then rescale(scale), then recolor, then appendChild INTO the slot? No — appending into instance is impossible. The helpers: iconBtn swaps the slot child; ic() used for free-standing icons (e.g., ch0 chevron in 10 — placed at frame level, recolored #667085).\n\nIn 10 I placed ch0 (Icon_Chevron_Down) at frame level — need screenshot to see if IT renders as glyph or square. Similarly sw (Icon_Swap) white on dark circle.\n\nLet me look at row 2 screenshots first (06-10), then do one read-only inspection to diagnose the icon rendering issue, then fix.\n\nActually — wait. NEW IDEA about the solid squares: swapComponent on a nested instance replaces it. The swapped-in instance may carry an \"absoluteRenderBounds\"... no. Rendering solid squares suggests the node rendering IS a filled rect. What if media icons like Icon_Menu are actually components whose content is a vector with FILL = solid color AND a rounded-rect mask/frame? At 24px a hamburger glyph has whitespace; the blob shows no whitespace.\n\nOR the blobs are my \"Badge Dot\"? No, badge is 10px red.\n\nOR — the Icon Btn component's child \"icon\" might be an instance of a component that itself contains a dark rounded-rect placeholder (\"icon slot\" placeholder = dark square showing where icon goes)?? If phase 2a created Icon Btn with child \"icon\" = a dark rounded-rect PLACEHOLDER (not a real icon), then when swap FAILED silently... but swaps returned successfully in builds (no errors). Unless swap() found name \"icon\" but the swap target comp(name) was null → swapComponent(null) would throw. Builds succeeded, so swap happened.\n\nHmm wait — did it? In 03 build the iconBtn helper: from summary \"iconBtn(f,name,x,y,dark) // swaps 'icon' child\". If comp(name) returned null, swapComponent would throw TypeError (like Coin/BNB did) and the build would fail — builds succeeded. So the icon instances ARE the right media components.\n\nSo media components like Icon_Menu, Icon_Contacts, Icon_Notification, Icon_History, Icon_More, Icon_Back, Icon_Chevron_Right, Icon_Car_Loan, Icon_Edit_Profile etc. render as SOLID ROUNDED SQUARES?? While Icon_Tab_* render as glyphs?? That's possible if the media page icons differ: Tab icons = line glyphs; others = maybe \"duotone filled\" style where the glyph is a rounded-square-ish filled shape. A hamburger menu icon drawn as filled style could be 3 stacked rounded bars = blob-ish. Chevron drawn filled = still an arrow shape though, not square.\n\nHonestly, need to inspect node structure. Let me screenshot row 2 AND run a read-only inspection in the same batch? Too