 Spotify logo = green circle frame + white glyph. If Logo_Apple = WHITE CIRCLE bg + dark glyph... it would render as white circle, not square. The screenshot shows white SQUARE with rounded corners ~ r8?\n\nHmm wait, look again at 09: From card logo area shows a white square ~24px. To card shows green circle. Also in 07 shortcut tiles: white squares. Icon Btn on dark = white squares. On light bank frames: dark squares. So the SQUARE color = the icon's own fill? If Icon_Back etc. are components that are just a VECTOR with fill... a vector renders as glyph not square.\n\nNEW HYPOTHESIS: The swap-in icon instances render at their ORIGINAL size but my rescale... The white squares in 07 tiles are ~20×20. In 03 top bar ~40×40 dark squares (Icon Btn size). Wait in 03 the WHOLE button is dark. If the button circle is white and icon is dark glyph... the screenshot showed whole 40px blob dark. Unless the Icon Btn root frame itself got recolored dark by my recolor walker! My recolor() walks children but SKIPS INSTANCE children. Icon Btn root frame is a FRAME → skipped at root? My recolor(node,paint): if node.type not in skip list → assign paints... wait the skip list INCLUDED FRAME. Let me recall: `recolor(n,p)` — \"skips FRAME/GROUP/COMPONENT/TEXT/INSTANCE/BOOLEAN_OPERATION\" — those types are SKIPPED (not painted, don't descend? or descend but not paint?). If it descends into frames to find vectors: Icon Btn = FRAME(circle white) + INSTANCE(icon). Descend: frame skipped as paint target but children visited?; icon instance → its children are vectors — if walker descends INTO instances (despite naming them skip?) it would paint the glyph vectors. That would make glyphs solid color — but glyphs are line shapes, painting them solid still shows glyph shape.\n\nThe rendering is SQUARE. A square = the icon vector itself is square-shaped?? For Icon_Menu (hamburger)? No.\n\nFORGET speculation — the inspection call FAILED with a weird error: \"node.componentId: no such property 'componentId' on INSTANCE node\" — interesting! In THIS environment, INSTANCE nodes DON'T have componentId?? That's unusual (real Figma API has componentId on instances). This sandbox's API differs. That also means my earlier comp() lookups and componentId filters in past builds worked because... I used findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.componentId===X) in rowByTicker during prototype wiring — and that SUCCEEDED (ok:21). Hmm, maybe the crash is on a non-INSTANCE node: findAll callback ran on nodes where node.componentId accessed but node is INSTANCE?? The error says INSTANCE node lacks componentId. But rowByTicker used componentId too and worked... Actually no — rowByTicker checked findOne(name===\"ticker\") inside instances, not componentId. The navTab used name===\"nav\". OK so in this environment INSTANCE.componentId does NOT exist. Use mainComponent instead? That may also not exist. Better: match by instance name (instances auto-named after component) or check n.mainComponent if available with try/catch.\n\nAlso note error came from `f3.findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.componentId===ibC.id)` — it crashed when n is INSTANCE (evaluating n.componentId). Weird but fine: restructure to use try/catch or name matching. Instance names: when I created instances via comp(\"X\").createInstance(), name defaults to component name \"X\". So findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"Icon Btn\").\n\nNow diagnose icon rendering. Re-run inspection with name-based matching and deeper dumps incl. fills of the icon instance and its children, plus check what Icon_Menu/Icon_Chevron_Right components contain, plus how the icon instance inside Icon Btn component (the master) looks.\n\nAlso inspect Logo_Apple component structure.\n\nPlan the inspection code:\n\n```js\nconst W=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"8:2\");\nconst f3=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"13:2\");\nconst f5=await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(\"15:2\");\nfunction jp(v){try{return JSON.stringify(v).slice(0,120)}catch(e){return \"?\"}}\nfunction dump(n,d){...as before...}\nconst ibInst=f3.findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"Icon Btn\")[0];\nconst ibIcon=ibInst?ibInst.children.find(c=>c.name===\"icon\"):null;\n// fills of ibIcon & children\nlet out=[];\nout.push(\"IBbtn:\"+dump(ibInst,1));\nout.push(\"IBicon:\"+dump(ibIcon,3));\nif(ibIcon&&ibIcon.children){out.push(\"IBicon0fills:\"+jp(ibIcon.children[0].fills)+\" strokes:\"+jp(ibIcon.children[0].strokes));}\nconst mn=W.findOne(x=>x.type===\"COMPONENT\"&&x.name===\"Icon_Menu\");\nout.push(\"CompMenu:\"+dump(mn,3));\nconst cr=W.findOne(x=>x.type===\"COMPONENT\"&&x.name===\"Icon_Chevron_Right\");\nout.push(\"CompChevR:\"+dump(cr,3));\nconst srInst=f5.findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"Setting Row\")[0];\nif(srInst){const tile=srInst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"tile\");const chev=srInst.findOne(n=>n.name===\"chev\");\nout.push(\"SRtile:\"+dump(tile,2));out.push(\"SRchev:\"+dump(chev,2));}\nconst ap=W.findOne(x=>x.type===\"COMPONENT\"&&x.name===\"Logo_Apple\");\nout.push(\"CompApple:\"+dump(ap,3));\nreturn out.join(\" || \").slice(0,4000);\n```\n\nAlso check the \"icon\" child inside comp(\"Icon Btn\") master — the master's icon child: what is it? If the master's icon child is an INSTANCE of some icon, and swap replaced it... The rendering square color: on dark frames icons show WHITE squares; on light frames (bank) icons show DARK squares. White/dark = maybe the glyph color. A square though!\n\nWAIT. Look at 07 tiles again: 8 white squares each ~20px with label below. If the icon instance were rendering the GLYPH it'd show shape. Square suggests... the icon instance has a FILL on its root?! If media icon components are built as: FRAME (24×24, no fill) + vector glyph — renders glyph. But if built as RECTANGLE with fill + ... no.\n\nHmm, ALTERNATIVE: the icons render as squares because the swap target instance retains a BACKGROUND fill from the placeholder? Or because I set fills on the INSTANCE root: instance.fills = [solid] would paint the whole instance bbox as a square! If my recolor(n,paint) assigned paints to INSTANCE nodes... my skip list included INSTANCE — did it? From summary: \"recolor walker (skips FRAME/GROUP/COMPONENT/TEXT/INSTANCE/BOOLEAN_OPERATION)\". If INSTANCE skipped, root instance never painted. But maybe the skip meant \"don't paint but DO descend\"? Descending into instance children (vectors) and painting them → glyph painted solid. Still glyph-shaped.\n\nUNLESS the media icons themselves are actually SOLID SQUARES in the media page! I.e., 04·Media's \"icons\" might be rendered as image placeholders — e.g., the icons were created from an SVG import that failed, leaving rounded-rect shapes?? But nav Tab icons render as glyphs — those came from... the Tab Bar component built in phase 2a — maybe I built tab icons as my own vectors, not media icons!\n\nI need facts. Run inspection.","signature":"f6ad80a3f0b040debacedac0"}],"id":"3daa3363-a497-468d-81c7-cb9214863ff6","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d351031-0fa6-4945-b5e3-9a2839717795","uuid":"7beb2da7-6865-426a-a3b1-9fc9c2555cc8","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:48:49.642Z","thinking_duration_ms":64200}
