{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting results:\n\n1. `IBmaster: COMPONENT(40x40)[INSTANCE(24x24)[VECTOR(18x18)]]` — the Icon Btn master has an \"icon\" child (an INSTANCE 24×24 containing a VECTOR 18×18). Wait, but dump didn't show names. The child instance is 24×24 with a vector inside. So the icon slot contains an icon instance, which contains a vector glyph. Structure looks NORMAL.\n\n2. `IBinst: null` — findAll on f3 with name===\"Icon Btn\" found NOTHING! So the top-bar buttons on 03 are NOT instances named \"Icon Btn\". Hmm! Maybe when I created instances I renamed them (e.g., \"menuBtn\")? In the 03 build, the iconBtn helper created instance and probably set name to something like \"menuBtn\". That's why findAll by component name fails. Fine.\n\n3. CompMenu: COMPONENT(24×24)[VECTOR(18×18)] — Icon_Menu is a 24×24 component with an 18×18 vector. Normal glyph component!\n\n4. CompChevR: COMPONENT(24×24)[VECTOR(8×13)] — chevron glyph vector. Normal.\n\n5. CompApple: 32×32 [VECTOR(29×32)] — apple glyph vector. Normal.\n\n6. CompSpot: 34×32 [VECTOR(33×32), VECTOR(24×15)] — spotify: outer + waves. Normal.\n\nSo components look structurally normal. But the master's icon INSTANCE child — what component is that instance of? The dump didn't show its name. VECTOR(18×18) inside — same structure as Icon_Menu (18×18 vector). So the master's icon child is an instance of some icon (maybe Icon_Menu default).\n\nSo why do they render as SOLID SQUARES?? Structure is component → vector. Unless... the VECTOR's FILL is fine but the swap... hold on. Let me reconsider what \"renders as white square\" means.\n\nIn 07 shortcut tiles: white squares ~20px. The tiles contain icon instances (swapped). The icon instances are 24×24 (rescaled?). A VECTOR with fills renders its geometry. UNLESS the vector has IMAGE fills that fail to render?? If the media page icons use IMAGE fills (e.g., imported SVGs converted to images?), and the fill image isn't loading in render, Figma might render... no, failed image renders as gray.\n\nWAIT — maybe the vector has fills = solid WHITE and STROKES, and the geometry is a glyph; rendering a hamburger as solid white 18×18?? The dump shows vector 18×18 — that's just its bbox; a hamburger glyph's bbox IS 18×18 (3 bars). It wouldn't render as full square.\n\nHmm, unless the vector path is BROKEN (e.g., path data lost) rendering as full-bbox square? That can happen if... unlikely.\n\nLet me look at screenshots again more carefully:\n\n07 tiles: white rounded squares, uniform. If glyph = white hamburger on dark bg at 18px scaled to ~20px, we'd see 3 bars. We see solid square. So the render = full bbox filled.\n\n09 delete key: white square. The Key/Del component's \"icon\" child = instance (from earlier dump: Key/Del → INSTANCE \"icon\").\n\n09 Apple logo: white SQUARE ~26px. Logo_Apple is a 32×32 vector glyph (apple silhouette with bite). Rendering as full square?!\n\n08 coin logos render FINE (BTC circle etc.) — those are Coin_* components with ellipse fills + letter TEXTs, not vector glyphs.\n\n07 center nav button \"Exchange\" renders its icon glyph fine! That icon came from... Trade Tab Bar component — its center button icon. It renders as glyph! So SOME vectors render fine (center exchange icon, sparklines are vectors? sparklines render fine, chevron in 10 renders? ch0 in 10 — screenshot 10 shows pair header: after \"BTC / USDT\" there's... I see text then prices; the chevron at 142,57 — can't discern. The swap circle in 09 renders as dark circle — can't tell if glyph inside.\n\nKEY OBSERVATION: vectors that render fine: sparkline strokes (polylines), center exchange icon (probably built by me manually), the ID card illustration in 02 (renders as blue rects — by design), viewfinder corners (vectors I made). The ones that DON'T render: ALL media-page glyph vectors (Icon_Menu, Icon_Chevron_Right, Logo_Apple...).\n\n=> The media-page icon VECTOR nodes likely have IMAGE PAINT fills (from SVG import as images?) or their fills are some paint type that renders as solid square (e.g., a PATTERN paint or an unloaded image). If fills = [{type:\"IMAGE\", ...}] and the image fails to render in screenshot export... would show as transparent, not white square. If fills=[{type:\"SOLID\"}] the vector geometry shows. A SOLID-filled vector renders glyph shape. So square render implies the fills aren't solid-on-glyph...\n\nHold on — maybe the icons aren't VECTORs with paths but RECTANGLES with image fills on the media page, and what I dumped as VECTOR(18×18) — hmm it says type VECTOR.\n\nA VECTOR node renders its vectorPaths/geometry. If vectorPaths = [] but vectorNetwork exists... it still renders.\n\nActually WAIT: maybe the vector's fill is a SOLID and the geometry is fine, but the icon instances are rendered at HUGE scale clipped?? No — sizes shown are right (24×24).\n\nLet me test differently: check the actual fills of the vector inside CompMenu master. My dump didn't print fills for these. Also check vectorPaths length. Also check `strokes`. Let me print fills/strokes/width/height of CompMenu.children[0], CompChevR.children[0], CompApple.children[0].\n\nALSO print the media page (1:4) master icons as they exist there — maybe W.findOne found COMPONENTS on workspace page (copies). Are these the same as media page assets? I created workspace-local components copied from media? In phase 2a I \"imported\" media assets by creating workspace copies? The summary says comp() name lookup on page 8:2. The icon components exist on the workspace page. Whether they were duplicated from 04·Media or rebuilt — the VECTOR fills matter.\n\nLet me also visually test: render Icon_Menu component itself via get_screenshot (nodeId of the component) — if the COMPONENT renders as a square, then it's a media asset problem; if it renders as hamburger, then the problem is in instance/override land (e.g., swap replacing with something weird).\n\nBetter plan: one call dumping fills of those vectors + screenshot of CompMenu node.\n\nActually a faster diagnostic: get_screenshot of the \"02 · Components\" page or of a single icon component node. Get CompMenu id and screenshot it. Let me do both in one batch: use_figma (returns ids + fills) then screenshot? Screenshot needs the id — dependency. Do use_figma first returning fills AND ids, then decide.\n\nActually, I can make the use_figma call also CREATE a temp test: no — keep read-only. Let me get fills + ids, then screenshot the component.","signature":"0bd9a392327940c08c41d109"}],"id":"05ccfe15-eff3-49b1-b113-2047e44b0f0d","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d351031-0fa6-4945-b5e3-9a2839717795","uuid":"3f2ace62-4ee3-40b3-b55e-b74ef2166e0d","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:49:46.599Z","thinking_duration_ms":36000}
