{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Icon_Menu component renders as a proper glyph (looks like a \"scan/frame\" style icon — two brackets and a line, i.e., an unusual menu icon but a GLYPH, dark #1A1A1F on white/transparent). NOT a square!\n\nSo components render fine standalone. But instances swapped into slots render as squares. The difference: in my frames, the icon instances were SWAPPED (swapComponent) and possibly RECOLORED and RESCALED.\n\nWait — actually, look at the 03 screenshot again: top-left button = dark blob ~40px. Icon Btn master: 40×40 frame (white circle?) + icon instance 24×24 (dark glyph). If the instance renders its glyph dark on the white circle... the screenshot showed the whole 40px area DARK. What if the Icon Btn root frame fill got changed to dark? On bank pages buttons looked DARK squares — root frame fill dark? My recolor walker skips FRAME for painting... but maybe it does NOT skip descending and the button frame was painted somewhere else. Hmm.\n\nOR the swap in this sandbox: swapComponent replaced the icon instance with the new component's instance — but maybe in this sandbox swapComponent COPIES THE PLACEHOLDER'S override fills onto the new instance?? The icon instance in the master had fills overridden? IconBtn.iconInst fills = SOLID dark (0.0627,0.0941,0.1568) = #101828. The icon INSTANCE ROOT has a fills override (dark #101828)!! An instance root with a SOLID FILL paints its whole bbox = SQUARE!\n\nThat's it! The icon instance node itself carries fills=[solid #101828] — instance-level fill override painting the full 24×24 bbox as a solid square, covering/behind the glyph. Where did that fill come from? Either the master's icon instance was created with a fill (my phase-2a build may have set fills on the instance root as a placeholder), or my recolor walker painted instance roots (walker skip list maybe didn't include INSTANCE at top level in some helper).\n\nAnd in the Icon Btn MASTER, the icon instance fills=#101828 (dark square!). On light bank frames, that renders as dark square 24×24 inside white 40 circle → screenshot showed dark blob w/ slight rounding. On dark trading frames: the SAME dark fill #101828 should blend into dark bg... but 07 tiles show WHITE squares. Hmm — those tile icons were probably recolored WHITE by my tile icon recolor (recolor walked into instance root? or set fills on the instance). If recolor painted the instance ROOT white → white square. And glyph remains dark or white underneath — invisible either way.\n\nSo the FIX: for every icon instance I swapped/placed, clear the instance ROOT fills (fills=[]) so only the inner vector glyph shows. The glyph inside keeps its own dark fill (or my recolor walker may have also painted inner vectors — good, that's how they get white on dark).\n\nWait but if recolor painted inner vectors too, glyph color = intended color. The square = instance-root fill. Removing root fills reveals glyph. \n\nBut hold on — does recolor walker paint inner vectors? If the walker skipped INSTANCE children entirely (skip list included INSTANCE → don't descend), glyphs keep original dark #1A1A1F. On dark trading frames, dark glyph on dark bg = invisible, plus white root square on top. After removing root fills: dark glyph invisible on dark bg — still wrong but different wrong. Need glyph color = intended (white on dark UI, brand/dark on light UI).\n\nHmm, what did my ic()/swap helpers do exactly? From summary: \"ic() used for free-standing icons (e.g., ch0 chevron in 10 — placed at frame level, recolored #667085)\". If recolor instance root got painted... ugh.\n\nLet me define the fix precisely:\n1. Find all instances of media icon components inside my 10 frames (they're nested in slots or free).\n2. For each: set instance.fills = [] (kill root square fill).\n3. For each: set the inner vector fill to the INTENDED color per context:\n   - Bank light frames (01–05): glyph #101828-ish dark (original dark is fine) — but what did I intend? Icon Btn on light: dark glyph. Tiles on light: brand blue icons on light-blue tile? In 03 screenshot tiles are solid blue — tile root fill also painted? Tile is a FRAME though... the tile in Txn Row master: FRAME \"tile\" fill #EAF2FF + icon instance. In screenshot, tile area = solid medium blue square. That's icon instance root painted #1573FE (brand) covering 44px?? tile is 44×44, icon 24×24 — but screenshot blue square looks ~40px. Hmm, maybe BOTH tile frame got painted blue AND icon root. My recolor(n,paint) when called with the ROW instance might have painted everything walkable: frames too? Skip list included FRAME... but maybe only at paint-time while still descending. Honestly the details are lost; the empirical evidence:\n   - squares of various colors = instance ROOT fills (painted by my helpers)\n   - tile backgrounds possibly also painted.\n\nRather than guessing each context color, simplest robust fix: for every icon instance within the 10 frames: fills=[] on the instance root, and repaint the innermost VECTOR glyphs by context:\n   - Frames 01–05 (light): glyph dark #101828. But tiles were meant as #EAF2FF tile + brand icon? In screenshot tiles are saturated blue — meaning tile frame fill ALSO painted brand. After fixing icon, tiles would still be blue background → need to restore tile fill #EAF2FF? Wait was the tile blue-by-design? My design: 44×44 tile #EAF2FF (light blue) with brand glyph. Screenshot: solid brand blue. So tile frame fill was overwritten to brand too. Restore tile fill to #EAF2FF and glyph to #1573FE.\n   - Nav bars: labels/icons — active #1573FE (bank) / #5AA2FF (trade), inactive #98A2B3 (bank) / #66758F (trade). Nav inactive icons rendered as WHITE SQUARES in 07/08/09/10 and dark squares in 03/04/05 — consistent with root-fill painting. After fix, glyphs recolor properly.\n   - Trading frames 06–10: glyph #F2F5F9 (white-ish) for top buttons, or specific: Icon Btn/Dark glyph white; Setting chevrons etc.\n   - Center Exchange nav icon: renders fine already (probably NOT an instance root fill issue because it was built manually as vector, not swapped instance).\n   - Logo_Apple white square: apple glyph dark; on dark card needs WHITE. Its instance root painted white → square. Fix: root fills=[], glyph → white.\n   - Logo_Spotify renders fine?? Its component has TWO vectors (outer green circle + waves) — root instance maybe fills=[] already or painted but the outer vector covers? It rendered correctly, so leave or apply same fix safely (root fills=[] harmless if already none).\n   - Coin logos render fine (ellipse+text, no instance-root fill).\n   - Sparklines fine (vectors I made).\n   - Key/Del icon → white glyph on dark key.\n   - Shortcut Tile icons → white glyphs.\n   - 02 back button icon → dark glyph (light circle).\n   - 09 steppers manual — fine.\n   - 10 View Toggle / Type Pill / Seg — fine.\n   - 05 notification switch — fine.\n   - 04 chart tooltip — fine.\n\nAlso possible: recolor painted inner vectors too — after root fills=[] the glyph shows in whatever color it has now (maybe already recolored correctly!). So plan: \nStep A (fix): for each of the 10 frames, walk all INSTANCE descendants; if instance has fills (non-empty) → set fills=[]. Then check glyph color: walk into instance children vectors; DON'T repaint yet — first re-screenshot to see what remains. Cheaper: do fills=[] pass + repaint vectors per-context in ONE pass, then screenshot.\n\nBut per-context repaint requires knowing each instance's intended color — complex. Alternative: rely on existing inner-vector colors: my recolor helpers probably DID repaint inner vectors when called on the icon (e.g., recolor(icn, white) → if walker descends into instance children, vectors became white). Evidence: 09 Spotify renders right; 07 center icon right. For top Icon Btns on dark frames I recolored icon white presumably → inner vector white → after root-fill removal, white glyph on dark circle = CORRECT. On bank frames icons recolored dark/brand presumably → correct.\n\nRisk: walker may NOT have descended into instances, leaving inner glyphs dark #1A1A1F. On dark frames those'd be invisible. To handle: in the same fix pass, after fills=[], check each icon instance's innermost vector fill: if it's the default dark #1A1A1F AND the frame context is dark trading UI → repaint white-ish per context. But \"per context\" hard programmatically... \n\nPragmatic approach: \n- Pass 1: clear ALL instance-root fills across the 10 frames (record count). Also fix tile frame fills if they were painted brand (restore #EAF2FF for Txn Row/Setting Row tiles? check first). Screenshot row 1 + row 2 to see result.\n- Pass 2: repaint remaining invisible glyphs per context as needed.\n\nAlso need to handle: the icon instance roots inside COMPONENT masters on workspace page (Icon Btn master's icon has fills #101828!). Fix masters too so future instances are clean. And the swap() helper instances created fresh — do fresh createInstance() of Icon_Menu have fills? Fresh instance root fills = none normally. The #101828 on master's icon suggests phase-2a explicitly set it OR the master was built by swapping an instance that already had fill override. Either way, clear fills on ALL icon-like instances in masters too.\n\nWhat about Setting Row tile: in 05 screenshot the tiles are brand-blue squares ~44px. Setting Row master: tile FRAME (#EAF2FF?) + icon. Screenshot blue = tile painted brand. Need to restore tile fill. Which frames painted? My bank build recolor... I'll inspect Setting Row/Txn Row master fills in fix pass and restore: tile fill #EAF2FF.\n\nAlso chevrons in Setting Row rows (05): right side dark squares ~16px → chev icon instance root painted dark; after fills=[] → chevron glyph dark #1A1A1F on white row — visible dark chevron = fine/correct look.\n\nTxn Row tiles: same restore #EAF2FF + glyph brand? Glyph currently brand (recolor walked in?) — if glyph painted brand, great: light-blue tile + brand glyph.\n\nNav bars bank: t0..t4 icons — dark squares in screenshots; after fills=[] → glyphs whatever color they were recolored to (#98A2B3/#1573FE if walker descended, else dark #1A1A1F). If dark on white bg — looks acceptable-ish but intended gray/blue. Check after pass 1.\n\nAlso 01_Welcome illustration and 06 coins: BTC/ETH coins in 06 render (BTC orange circle top right, ETH left) — those are Coin components w/ ellipses — fine.\n\n07 banners: left banner text card renders with weird copy (\"What is The... Versus is WooG?\" garbled) — that's a Swap Card / promo banner component with text overrides; acceptable? The right banner = colorful \"UP TO 50% OFF\" graphic — probably a media IMAGE asset (Banner_50 or similar). It looks garish but it IS the media asset. Hmm, \"UP TO 50% OFF COUPONS\" image — it's likely from 04·Media. Since brief says reuse media assets, acceptable. But wait — is that actually what I placed, or is it a broken image render? It renders colorful — likely an image fill from media (Coupon banner). Leave as is.\n\nAlso 07 top-right: TWO white squares (notification + more buttons). After fix → dark circles w/ glyphs.\n\n07 search bar fine. Avatar renders (pink circle w/ face illustration) fine.\n\n07 portfolio rows: good. Sparklines: BTC green, ETH red? screenshot shows BTC green wiggle, ETH red, XRP green, BNB green — mixed per chg signs. fine.\n\n08: filter white square → fix. Coin rows all good. Nav squares → fix.\n\n09: filter/calc white squares; Apple logo white square; chevron-down in From card missing-ish (small white square next to AAPL? I see \"AAPL\" then dash-ish); Key/Del white square; nav squares → fix. Swap circle: renders dark circle — glyph inside? can't tell; after fills=[] check.\n\n10: pair header Coin_BTC renders; \"+3.73% 29,198.24\" top right — WAIT, in screenshot top-right shows \"+3.73% 29,198.24\" CRAMMED together: \"+3.73%29,198.24\"? It shows \"+3.73% 29,198.24\" — price left of pct? My layout: price right-aligned w120 at x280..400? price box x=280 w120 → right edge 400 (offscreen 390!). Screenshot: \"+3.73%\" then \"29,198.24\" to its right — overlapping edge. Actually shows \"+3.73%29,198.24\" at top right, slightly cut? Looks like pct at far right and price left of it — hmm order swapped from my code (price x280 w120 right-edge 400, pct x284 w70 right-edge 354) — overlapping boxes! price right edge should be 390-16=374. I set x280 → 280+120=400 = 10px offscreen. Fix: price x=254 w120 → right edge 374; pct x=284 w70 → right edge 354... still overlap with price box but right-aligned text: price text ends at 374, pct text ends at 354 — pct would overlap price's box but visually pct sits left of price?? In screenshot they read \"+3.73% 29,198.24\" left-to-right = pct LEFT, price RIGHT. But pct box right edge 354 vs price right edge 374 → pct text right-aligned ends 354, price right-aligned ends 374 → price extends further right, pct to its left. Screenshot consistent. Slight overlap of boxes but texts don't collide since right-aligned. BUT price box extends 10px offscreen; text right-aligned at 400?? Wait right-aligned text in a box ending at 400 → text ends at 400 = 10px clipped offscreen. Screenshot shows \"29,198.24\" fully visible though... close to edge. Actually \"+3.73% 29,198.24\" — hmm price ends ~edge-8. Might be okay-ish but should fix: set price x=254.\n\nActually wait, look again at 10 screenshot top right: \"+3.73% 29,198.24\" — hmm no, it shows \"+3.73%\" ABOVE \"29,198.24\"? No, single line. Fine — I'll fix price box to x=254 w120 (right edge 374) and pct x=244 w70 (right edge 314)? That puts pct text ending at 314, price starting after. Visually: \"…29,198.24  +3.73%\"? Which order is standard? Price then change. Screenshot currently: \"+3.73% 29,198.24\" pct LEFT of price?? That reads odd. Standard: price left, pct right. I'll set: price box x=200 w120 (right edge 320) hmm but then gap to pct at right edge 374... Let me: pct right edge 374 (x=304,w70),