nstances where I INTENTIONALLY set root fill? Did I? 09 swapCircle is an ellipse (not instance). 10 manual steppers use ellipses. whiteChip in 08: white ellipse at frame level. I don't think any instance root fill was intentional. There's risk with \"Search\" instances? Search bar = component with frame bg (not instance root). Nav center button? built into tab bar component.\n\nAlso masters on page: icon instances inside COMPONENT masters (Icon Btn, Txn Row, Setting Row, Key/Del, Shortcut Tile, Type Pill, Coin Row's logo instance, etc.) also have root fills? The master IconBtn.iconInst HAS fills #101828 — instances inherit that. Clearing in frames handles the 10 screens; masters should be cleaned too so components stay reusable. I'll ALSO walk all COMPONENT nodes on page 8:2 and clear instance-root fills inside them. BUT careful: masters like \"Coin Row\" contain logo INSTANCE of Coin_BTC — if that instance root has a fill (unlikely)... clearing harmless.\n\nEXCEPT: careful with instances whose root fill IS the design: e.g., \"Type Pill\" instance root fill? If Type Pill component = frame bg. Instance root = the pill instance itself — if component root frame has fill, instances DON'T duplicate it as instance-root fills (fills on instance node itself are overrides; default instance node fills = [] typically? Actually in Figma, instance nodes inherit root component fills — the instance node's .fills returns the inherited value! So clearing instance.fills where the COMPONENT ROOT has a bg fill would BREAK it!).\n\nHmm! Instance.fills returns the fill of the main component's root if not overridden. So IconBtn.iconInst fills=#101828 — is that inherited from Icon_Menu's COMPONENT root?? Icon_Menu component = 24×24 with child vector — component root fill = none? If root fill none, inherited fills = []. But iconInst fills = #101828 → that's an OVERRIDE (set somewhere). For icon instances: main = Icon_Menu etc. whose component roots have NO fill → inherited fills=[] → any non-empty fills on the instance = override = the square. SAFE to clear for icon instances.\n\nBut for instances like Pct Chip (component root frame w/ bg #1A2232): instance.fills returns inherited #1A2232 (non-empty!) → clearing would make pill transparent! DANGER.\n\nSo I must only clear fills on instances whose main component root has NO fill. Check: ins.mainComponent && mainComponent fills empty → clear override. In this sandbox mainComponent may not exist (componentId missing!). Test needed: does ins.mainComponent work? The debug earlier: \"node.componentId: no such property on INSTANCE\". mainComponent might also be missing. Alternative: infer by size! Icon instances are 14–32px squares. Pct Chip 75×28, Type Pill ~100×28, Search wide, rows big. Heuristic: clear fills only if width<=34 && height<=34. Icon instances rescaled: 24, 20, 16, 14, 32 (apple 32×30), 18 (swap), 24 del. Chip/pill widths ≥70. Coin logos in rows: rescaled to 40 or 24... Coin_BTC instance 40×40 — has fills? Coin component root = frame w/ transparent bg? If Coin root fill none → inherited [] → no-op. White square? Coin logos RENDER fine so no fill override. But XRP whiteChip: I hid logo + added white ellipse separately — fine.\n\nSo heuristic: INSTANCE && w<=34 && h<=34 && fills.length>0 → fills=[]. This clears icon squares (16–32px) without touching chips/pills/rows. Type Pill \"ch\" chip instance — small? Type Pill master: TEXT \"t\" + INSTANCE \"ch\" — ch is probably a small chevron instance ~16px → cleared. Good.\n\nAlso masters: walk COMPONENTs' instance descendants with same rule.\n\nTile restore: Txn Row/Setting Row tile frames painted brand-blue. Find instances of \"Txn Row\"/\"Setting Row\" in f3,f4,f5 → findOne(name===\"tile\") → set fills=[#EAF2FF]. Can I set fills INSIDE instance subtree? tile is a FRAME inside instance — setting fills on children inside instances IS allowed (only layout/transform restricted). Earlier error was relative-transform only. fills override allowed. \n\nBu