d icon instance + vector → vs from the Key/Del root = 1 vector (since nested icon is INSTANCE) → w=70 excluded... but the nested icon instance itself is in the outer findAll list (nested) → w=24, its vectors=1 → white. \n\nApple: instance w=40, vs=1 → white. IconBtn instances: icon nested handled separately (icon w=24 vs=1 → white). Spotify w=40, vs=2 → skip. Filter icon w24 vs1 → white. Calc icon w24 → white. Chevron-down w=14 → excluded (<18). \n\nBut this whites EVERY small icon in f9 — includes none else. Fine.\n\nSimilarly f10? 10 icons: ch0 chevron #667085 (14, skip), sw swap white 18 → w18 vs? Icon_Swap may have 1 vector → white ✓ (intended white). steppers minus/plus manual — not instances? I used Icon_Minus/Icon_Plus instances at frame level (w14) → skip — but they were placed white already? Screenshot 10 shows minus/plus visible white ✓. View Toggle/Pct chips fine. Nav icons: inactive gray... nav icons are nested in nav INSTANCE → they're instances w~20 → pass1 clears root; white-pass would make them WHITE but inactive should be #66758F! So NO blanket white-pass on f10. Only f9 gets white-pass? f9 nav icons also would get whitened! Exclude nav: skip instances whose parent chain includes name \"nav\". Implement: collect navInstance=f9.findOne(n=>n.name===\"nav\") and its findAll set; exclude from white pass. Ugh complexity. Alternative: don't white-pass nav icons; keep them — after pass1, glyph colors unknown (maybe already colored during build via recolor descent).\n\nDECISION: Run pass1 (fills clear) + tiles + header fix ONLY. Screenshot 2 frames (03, 09). Then decide color passes with evidence.\n\nActually include apple+keydel white in f9 but EXCLUDE nodes under nav (name check up-chain: walk parent until frame root; if any parent.name===\"nav\" skip). Simple loop. And f10: leave glyphs; screenshot will tell.\n\nLet me finalize code with parent-chain check for f9 white pass:\n\n```js\nfunction underNav(n){let p=n.parent;while(p){if(p.name===\"nav\")retur