ed. Get ids + screenshot in 2 steps.\n\n3. **filterBtn/calcBtn** (f9): fills = DARK #1A1A22-ish (0.10,0.13) ✓ dark root — correct for Icon Btn/Dark! But 09 screenshot showed WHITE squares at those positions! With dark root + white glyph, render should be dark circle + glyph. Screenshot shows WHITE square ~28px. CONTRADICTION → the white square is NOT the button root; it's the ICON inside (icon instance 24px, root cleared, inner vector...). For f9 I whitened 1-vector icons (white=7): filter icon got whitened ✓ → white GLYPH on dark button = correct final look. But screenshot (taken AFTER pass A) showed white SQUARES at filter/calc — hmm, but wait, 09 screenshot was taken AFTER pass A... and showed white squares ~28px at filter position (334,54) and calc (334,100). If those were white GLYPHS they'd have shape (funnel/calculator). Square = full-bbox render.\n\nSo the inner VECTOR of these icons renders as FULL SQUARE despite vectorPaths glyph?! But Icon_Menu component screenshot rendered glyph fine... \n\nHmm hm hm. Wait — Icon_Menu standalone render = glyph ✓. Icon_Deposit instance inner vector fills=white. What if THESE particular icon components (Icon_Deposit, Icon_Filter, Icon_Calculator, Icon_Notification...) have vector paths that ARE squares?? Different icons, different paths! Icon_Menu happened to be a real glyph. Maybe the media page's OTHER icons are broken/square!\n\nEvidence: 09's whitened icons: apple (renders white APPLE ✓ — glyph!), del (renders del glyph ✓), swap (renders ✓). Those work! Filter/calc show squares. Apple=Logo_Apple 1 vector ✓ glyph. So SOME icons glyph, SOME square → per-icon difference → the square ones have square path data!\n\nCheck: Icon_Filter vector path — is it a funnel? Media page Icon_Filter 24×24 [VECTOR 18×18]. A funnel glyph path would have distinct shape. If its vectorPaths = [M0 0 L18 0 L18 18 L0 18 Z] → square!\n\nWAIT — why would media icons be squares? OH!!! I bet I know — during phase-2a asset import, maybe I RECREATED the icons as rounded-rect placeholders for some, or the SVG import produced rects for multi-path icons (flattened?). Whatever the cause, fix = REPLACE the square-path vectors with real glyphs? That's heavy. ALTERNATIVE: verify which icons are square by screenshotting the icon components from media page quickly (batch a few).\n\nTest batch: screenshot Icon_Filter (9:32), Icon_Notification (9:22), Icon_Deposit (need id), Icon_Scan (9:30) — 4 tiny screenshots. Icon_Scan was in my earlier fills dump (9:30). If they render as squares → media assets themselves are squares → I should REPLACE those glyph vectors with hand-drawn simple glyphs (lines/paths) OR accept? NO — brief requires quality; draw proper glyphs.\n\nHmm wait, actually — before heavy work: reconsider. 07 shortcut icons ALL render as white squares. 8 different icons (Deposit/Earn/Gift/More/Orders/Referal/Save/Shop) ALL square?? If media icons were mostly broken squares, then 03's menu button (Icon_Menu) worked because Icon_Menu happens to be real. Apple works. Swap works. Del works. Chevrons? 09 chevron-down in From card — screenshot shows tiny dash — maybe renders as tiny square?? At 14px hard to tell.\n\nLet me check vectorPaths data directly for a few: Icon_Filter (9:32), Icon_Notification (9:22), Icon_Deposit, Icon_Notification... vectorPaths path data strings! If path = \"M 0 0 L 18 0 L 18 18 L 0 18 Z\" → square confirmed. Read vectorPaths[0].path (truncate 100 chars) for: Icon_Filter, Icon_Notification, Icon_Menu (control), Icon_Deposit, Icon_Earn, Icon_Scan, Icon_Back, Icon_Chevron_Right (control glyph 8×13).\n\nThat's decisive. Then fix = redraw squares as proper glyphs via vectorPaths replacement (set vectorPaths on vectors — allowed via setVectorNetworkAsync? vectorPaths is settable? In plugin API, vectorPaths is settable on VectorNode). I can set simple glyph paths (lines with stroke? or filled paths). Easier: replace vector with multiple RECTANGLES/LINES/Ellipses arranged as glyph (e.g., filter funnel = 3 lines? Standard filter = funnel triangle lines). But nodes inside COMPONENT masters can be edited freely ✓. Instances inherit.\n\nPlan: read path data → identify square icons → rebuild those components' vector into glyph approximations (using simple shapes: rects/ellipses/lines/polygons via createPolygon? or vectorPaths with hand-authored path strings). Hand-authoring path strings for ~10 icons is doable: menu(3 lines), filter(funnel), notification(bell), scan(corner brackets+line), deposit(down arrow into tray?), earn(coin?), gift(box), more(3 dots), orders(doc lines), referal(person+), save(piggy/bank), shop(bag), calculator, back(arrow), search(magnifier — renders? search icon inside search bar at 64,52 — 07 screenshot search icon shows as circle glyph ✓ visible!), currency, history, car/mortgage/personal loan icons (03 txn rows rendered BLUE GLYPHS ✓ — they work!), key del ✓, chevrons ✓...\n\nWait 03 txn row icons RENDER as glyphs (blue car etc. visible) — so loan icons fine.\n\nMake the inventory list first via vectorPaths read. Also possible: those \"square\" vectors have fills but ALSO the path might use fill-rule with even-odd creating glyph... the standalone Icon_Menu rendered fine so path data works for it.\n\nLet me read path data now.","signature":"292d19f0001746d9954d4392"}],"id":"5efe36be-c553-470f-bd0d-db8b48057161","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d351031-0fa6-4945-b5e3-9a2839717795","uuid":"f4a040db-a5ca-4882-8d7b-c7646a2440b5","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:57:37.160Z","thinking_duration_ms":53044}
