rom? Maybe the loan icon components were ALREADY blue on media page (no override), and my recolor skip-list actually skipped instance descendants (so no override applied). Then: working icons = NO overrides; broken icons = HAVE overrides (fill overrides on nested vector or instance root). The square = corruption caused by APPLYING an override to a nested vector/instance root!\n\nTest: in test frame, add i6: fresh Icon_Notification, then set its inner vector fills=blue → screenshot. If square → CONFIRMED: fill override on nested vector corrupts rendering in this sandbox.\n\nAnd the instance-root fills=[] clear on nested instance — also suspect. Add i7: fresh icon instance with root fills=[] → screenshot.\n\nIf confirmed, the FIX for all broken icons: REPLACE the corrupted node with a fresh instance — impossible inside instances... BUT the corruption might be removable by REVERSING the override? E.g., set the vector's fills back to the ORIGINAL component color (dark #1A1A1F)? If rendering is corrupted by the OVERRIDE ITSELF (any fill override on that node), resetting to identical value may not clear the \"overridden\" flag. There might be API to RESET an override? Not directly in plugin API (no resetOverride). BUT: swapping the corrupted child... can't touch children of instances.\n\nHmm wait — CAN I though? Earlier established: cannot appendChild into instance; cannot set relative-transform inside instance. But REMOVE a child from an instance? And can I modify a nested vector's other props? If I can REMOVE the corrupted vector from the nested instance and append a FRESH instance of the icon component INTO the nested instance... appendChild into instance = forbidden (error earlier). \n\nBUT — masters! For instances whose corruption came from MASTER-level overrides (Type Pill ch, Setting Row chev, Key/Del icon?): fix the MASTER (remove corrupted child, append fresh) → instances inherit fixed master content IF the per-instance overrides don't pin the old node. Instance-