{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting findings:\n\n1. **Broken icons** all show: instance root has a FILL (e.g., f:S(16,24,40) dark, or f:S(242,245,249) white) on the 24×24 icon instance. **Working icons** (menuBtn, sc0) show: icon instance root fills EMPTY (`f:` = empty string from `[]`).\n\nSo the pattern is clear now! The icon instance ROOT having a solid fill = renders as a SQUARE. When root fills=[] it renders the glyph.\n\nBut wait — test i7/i9 (root fills=[]) rendered glyph, and i6 (nested fill override) also rendered glyph... Hmm, i6 had BLUE fill on the inner VECTOR, not on the instance ROOT. The tests never tested a FILL ON THE INSTANCE ROOT! i7/i9 were root fills=[] (cleared). i6 was vector fills. i10 was strokes.\n\nSo: **fill on the instance ROOT (24×24 icon instance) renders as a solid square**, because the instance root is a container with a fill — it paints its whole bbox! Of course! An instance root is like a frame — setting a fill on it paints the entire bounding box. The glyph is inside, but the dark/white square fill covers the whole 24×24 box.\n\nWait, but then why did Pass A (clearing fills on all INSTANCE ≤34×34) not fix these? Let me check: Pass A cleared 39 instance fills. These still have fills: backBtn icon f:S(16,24,40)... \n\nOh wait! Look at menuBtn in 13:2: `1 INSTANCE icon 24x24 f:` — cleared! That's why menuBtn renders fine. And contactsBtn/notifBtn still have f:S(16,24,40). So Pass A cleared SOME but not all? Pass A said cleared=39, errs=0. Hmm, but these weren't cleared...\n\nWait — maybe Pass A's condition `n.fills.length>0` with the check `n.fills&&n.fills!==\"mixed\"` — these have fills. Why weren't they cleared? Maybe Pass A ran on a filtered subset? Or maybe Pass A's findAll crashed partway? It reported errs=0 though. Or maybe Pass A only walked certain frames/subtrees — \"cleared fills on all INSTANCE ≤34×34 within 10 frames + inside masters\". Hmm.\n\nWait, actually re-read: Pass A also \"whitened single-VECTOR instances 18–40px in f9\" — and here f9 filterBtn/calcBtn icon instances HAVE white fills S(242,245,249) — the whitening step may have SET fills on these icon instances (thinking they were single-vector instances 18-40px?). The icon instance is 24×24 — within 18-40px. If the whitening logic set fills=[white] on icon INSTANCE roots (not just vectors), that would CREATE squares! And similarly Pass A's clearing may have been applied then some later step re-added fills.\n\nHmm, but regardless of history: the fix is now obvious — **clear fills on the icon instance roots** (set fills=[] on INSTANCE nodes that host a single VECTOR child and have size ≤40). The working samples (menuBtn f: empty, sc0 icon f: empty) confirm cleared root = glyph renders.\n\nBut wait — one contradiction: f7 sc1 icon has f:S(242,245,249) — is sc1 broken? The summary said sc0–sc7 tile icons broken. sc0 has f: (cleared) but... was sc0 fixed by Pass A and sc1 not? count:8 found. Whatever — clear all.\n\nAlso f10 pill: no instance named \"pill\" found in 24:2 (res[\"24:2\"]=[] empty). And f5SR count:0 — no instances with name containing \"Setting\" in 15:2. Hmm. The Setting Rows in f5 and the pill in f10 must have different names. I need to enumerate instances in f5 and f10.\n\nAlso mastersTP: no component named \"Type Pill\" on page 1:3 — maybe named differently (\"Type/Pill\"? or it's a COMPONENT SET?). I'll enumerate.\n\nPlan for next call:\n1. Clear fills on ALL INSTANCE nodes ≤40×40 within the 10 frames that have non-empty fills — but EXCLUDE instances where the fill is intentional (tile fills on Txn Row/Setting Row are on the ROW instance itself, 343×64 — those are >40 so safe; icon instances inside are ≤40). Wait — also the 76×64 sc tiles are >40, fine. The 22×22 icon inside sc — clear. The 24×24 icons — clear. What about legitimately filled small instances? E.g., unread dot 10px red circle — that's an ELLIPSE not instance. Coin icons 22×22? In f7 watchlist, coin avatars are instances of Coin_BTC etc. — 36×36? If I clear their fills... Coin components: the coin logo components are 24×24 vectors with colored fills? If the coin instance root has a fill, clearing it is safe (root fill would be a square anyway). Actually wait — careful: are the coin avatars instance roots WITH fills that render correctly? In screenshots, coin logos rendered fine (f6/f8 confirmed good). If a coin instance root had a fill, it would render as a square — but they render fine, so either their roots have no fill or they're not instances. Clearing empty/no-op fills is harmless.\n\nBut one danger: clearing fills on instances like \"Txn Row\" (343 wide) — excluded by ≤40 size filter. Good. What about \"Pct Chip\" (small)? In f7 there are pct chips with green/red fills — are they instances? \"Pct Chip text child named t\" from earlier. If Pct Chip is a COMPONENT instance ~60×24 with a green fill — clearing its fill would BREAK the design (chip loses background)! Size 60 wide > 40? Maybe. Risky.\n\nSafer targeted approach: clear fills ONLY on instances named \"icon\" (that's the name inside buttons and sc tiles!) with size ≤40. From the dump, every broken icon child is named exactly \"icon\". menuBtn's working icon is also named \"icon\" with f: — consistent.\n\nSo: for each of the 10 frames, findAll(n=>n.type===\"INSTANCE\"&&n.name===\"icon\"&&n.width<=40&&n.height<=40) → set fills=[]. Count them.\n\nThat covers: f2 backBtn icon, f3/f4/f5 buttons' icons, f7 scanBtn/notifBtn/sc0-7 icons, f8/f9 filterBtn/calcBtn icons. \n\nWait but will clearing the icon root fill actually FIX rendering? The square comes from root fill painting bbox. Clearing removes the square, leaving the vector glyph inside with its own fill. The vector glyphs have their own fills (S(16,24,40) or white) — good, glyph will show in right color.\n\nBut hold on — why did menuBtn render fine AFTER Pass A while contactsBtn didn't, when Pass A claims to have cleared all? Maybe Pass A actua