n0-2 (big), nav (big) → ≤40: menuBtn, contactsBtn, notifBtn, unread ✓ matches byName (menuBtn1, contactsBtn1, notifBtn includes f3...).\n- f4: historyBtn?, notifBtn, unread... f4 might have historyBtn+currBtn? currBtn×1 in byName — maybe f4 has currBtn (currency button top-left?). dots×1 — f4 has a \"dots\" 3-dot button!\n- f5 top: historyBtn, moreBtn, notifBtn, unread, avatar(64>40? avatar 64x64 EXCLUDED... but byName HAS avatar×1 — from f7! f7 has avatar 64? no, 64>40. Hmm, avatar×1 — maybe f5's avatar is 64x64 — excluded. So which frame has ≤40 avatar? Maybe f3 has small avatar? Or f6?\n- Icon_Chevron_Down×1, Icon_Food×1, Icon_Ticket×1 — top-level instances somewhere (f3 txn rows use these as top-level? no, txn rows are instances... maybe f3's txn rows are FRAMES with Icon_* instances as direct children! That fits: txn0-2 might be frames, each containing Icon_Food/Icon_Ticket/Icon_Chevron_Down top-level within the row frame → findAll from frame root finds them if traversal is 2 levels... hmm.\n- coin×3, logo×2, swapIcon×1, pairLogo×1, pairChev×1, mi×2, pi×2 — f9/f10 top-level.\n- scanBtn×1 (f7), filterBtn×2 (f8,f9), calcBtn×1 (f9), backBtn×1 (f2), i×1 (?), chev×2 (??).\n\nSo THIS run = SHALLOW-ish (found top-level + maybe one level down: Icon_Food inside txn row frame...). The enumeration run = DEEP. SAME API?! \n\nUnless... the enumeration ran on f5 which I fetched fresh, while THIS run... also fetched each frame fresh. \n\nYou know what — maybe the difference is findAll callback complexity? Enumeration: x=>x.type===\"INSTANCE\". This run: same. Identical!!\n\nWAIT. Actually — is it possible the file was DIFFERENT between runs? Between the enumeration run and this run, I ran... nothing (this was the next call). File same.\n\nHmm, actually let me look again at THIS run's code: \n\n```js\nlet insts=[];try{insts=fr.findAll(x=>x.type===\"INSTANCE\");}catch(e){notes.push(\"FE\"+fid);continue;}\nfor(const ic of insts){try{if(ic.width>40||ic.height>40)continue;...\n```