itch exclusion (44x26 — but size filter ≤40 excludes it anyway ✓ since 44>40). Avatar 64 excluded ✓. Buttons 40x40 INCLUDED by size — must exclude by name: skip trimmed names ending in \"Btn\", plus \"unread\",\"dots\",\"logo\",\"pairLogo\",\"coin\",\"swapIcon\",\"avatar\",\"i\"?? \n\nHmm wait — what is \"i\"? And are there legit filled small instances I'd wrongly clear? Rule: only clear when trimmed name ∈ ICONS set {icon, mi, pi, ch, chev, editIcn, pairChev} — everything else SKIP (just log). With manual recursion I'll get the true full inventory; log all skipped ≤40 instances with fills for review.\n\nNote: buttons (backBtn etc.) have LEGIT fills — skipping by name ✓. \"coin\"×3 — coin avatars ≤40 with fills?? If coin instances have root fills... in f9 there are coin instances 24-ish? Clearing coin root fills — the coin logo is inner vector; root fill would be square → if present, it's a bug too. But name \"coin\" not in ICONS → skipped, logged for review. Fine — visual check will tell.\n\nAlso \"swapIcon\" f9 — the swap arrows icon; earlier pass whitened it and it rendered ✓. If it has root fill it'd be square — it rendered fine, so probably empty. Skipped+logged.\n\nAlso — for ROW blue glyphs: with manual recursion, find instances whose parent is row/brow → they're named \"icon\" → clear root + blue vector ✓.\n\nLet me also reconsider: maybe I should ALSO just directly fix via the WALKED nodes from f5i knowledge: I know exact hosts. But manual recursion generalizes to all frames — better.\n\nOne more trap: children of INSTANCE in this sandbox — walk() successfully descended (\"1 INSTANCE icon 24x24...2 VECTOR...\") ✓.\n\nAlso recursion into nav instance (contains 5 icon instances) ✓ fine.\n\nPotential DOUBLE-counting: nested instances appear once each ✓.\n\nCode:\n\n```js\nfunction firstVec(n){if(n.type===\"VECTOR\")return n;if(n.children){for(let i=0;i<n.children.length;i++){const r=firstVec(n.children[i]);if(r)return r;}}return null;}\nconst BLUE=[{type:\"SOL